:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Copyright Quartz Systems 2026.
:HELP NAME=ADDPFCST.Add Physical File Constraint (ADDPFCST)
:P.Use the Add Physical File Constraint (ADDPFCST) command to add a
unique, primary key, referential or check constraint to a physical file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPFCST/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPFCST/TYPE'.Constraint type (TYPE)
:P.The constraint type for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *REFCST, *UNQCST, *PRIKEY, *CHKCST.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPFCST/CST'.Constraint name (CST)
:P.The constraint name for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*GEN:EPK.
:PD.Generated by the system.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 258 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPFCST/KEY'.Key (KEY)
:P.The key for this command.
:P.Up to 120 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPFCST/PRNFILE'.Parent file (PRNFILE)
:P.The parent file for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPFCST/PRNKEY'.Parent key (PRNKEY)
:P.The parent key for this command.
:P.Up to 120 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PRNFILE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPFCST/DLTRULE'.Delete rule (DLTRULE)
:P.The delete rule for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NOACTION, *CASCADE, *SETNULL, *SETDFT,
*RESTRICT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPFCST/UPDRULE'.Update rule (UPDRULE)
:P.The update rule for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NOACTION, *RESTRICT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPFCST/CHKCST'.Check constraint (CHKCST)
:P.The check constraint for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 2000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ADDPFM.Add Physical File Member (ADDPFM)
:P.Use the Add Physical File Member (ADDPFM) command to add a member to
a physical file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPFM/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPFM/MBR'.Member (MBR)
:P.The member for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPFM/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPFM/EXPDATE'.Expiration date for member (EXPDATE)
:P.The date after which the object or file can be deleted or
overwritten. *PERM means it never expires.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.It never expires.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPFM/SHARE'.Share open data path (SHARE)
:P.Whether the open data path of the file is shared with other programs
of the job that open it with SHARE(*YES)&colon. they then share the
file's position and buffers.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The program gets an open data path of its own.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The open data path is shared.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPFM/SRCTYPE'.Source type (SRCTYPE)
:P.The type of the source member&colon. CLLE, RPGLE, PF, CMD and so on.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ADDPFTRG.Add Physical File Trigger (ADDPFTRG)
:P.Use the Add Physical File Trigger (ADDPFTRG) command to add a trigger
to a physical file&colon. a program the system calls whenever a record
of the file is inserted, deleted, updated or read, before or after the
change, in the job that makes it.
:P.The program gets two parameters&colon. the trigger buffer, with the
file's name, the event, the time and the record before and after the
change, and the buffer's length. A before trigger that ends in an escape
message stops the change. The trigger is in effect from the next open of
the file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPFTRG/FILE'.Physical file (FILE)
:P.The physical file the trigger is added to, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPFTRG/TRGTIME'.Trigger time (TRGTIME)
:P.Whether the program is called before or after the change. A read
trigger is always called after the read.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*BEFORE:EPK.
:PD.Before the reference entry.
:PT.:PK.*AFTER:EPK.
:PD.After the reference entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPFTRG/TRGEVENT'.Trigger event (TRGEVENT)
:P.The change that calls the program&colon. a record inserted, deleted,
updated or read.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*DELETE:EPK.
:PD.Deleted.
:PT.:PK.*READ:EPK.
:PD.Read authority.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *INSERT, *UPDATE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPFTRG/PGM'.Program (PGM)
:P.The trigger program, by name and library. It must exist when the
trigger is added.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPFTRG/RPLTRG'.Replace trigger (RPLTRG)
:P.Whether a trigger of the same name and library on the file is
replaced. A replaced trigger keeps its place in the order the file's
triggers are called.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPFTRG/TRG'.Trigger (TRG)
:P.The trigger's name, up to 128 characters. *GEN gives it a name made
of QSYS_TRIG_, the library, the file and a number.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*GEN:EPK.
:PD.Generated by the system.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 258 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPFTRG/TRGLIB'.Trigger library (TRGLIB)
:P.The library the trigger's name belongs to. *FILE is the file's
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPFTRG/ALWREPCHG'.Allow repeated change (ALWREPCHG)
:P.Whether the program may change the record&colon. a before trigger's
change of the new record in the buffer is written to the file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPFTRG/TRGUPDCND'.Trigger update condition (TRGUPDCND)
:P.For an update trigger&colon. whether the program is called for every
update, or only when the update changes the record.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALWAYS:EPK.
:PD.Always.
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPFTRG/THDSAFE'.Threadsafe (THDSAFE)
:P.Whether the trigger program is safe to call in a job with several
threads. It is kept for the catalogs.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *UNKNOWN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPFTRG/MLTTHDACN'.Multithreaded job action (MLTTHDACN)
:P.What happens when the trigger is called in a job with several
threads. It is kept for the catalogs.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*MSG:EPK.
:PD.A message is sent.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NORUN, *RUN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGLF.Change Logical File (CHGLF)
:P.Use the Change Logical File (CHGLF) command to change a logical
file's attributes.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGLF/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGLF/SYSTEM'.System (SYSTEM)
:P.The system for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LCL:EPK.
:PD.Local.
:PT.:PK.*RMT:EPK.
:PD.Remote.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FILETYPE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGLF/MAXMBRS'.Maximum members (MAXMBRS)
:P.The largest number of members the file can hold.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGLF/ACCPTHSIZ'.Access path size (ACCPTHSIZ)
:P.The largest size the file's access paths can reach.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MAX1TB, *MAX4GB.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGLF/PAGESIZE'.Access path logical page size (PAGESIZE)
:P.The size of a page of the keyed access path, in kilobytes.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *KEYLEN.
:P.The value must be 8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256, 512.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGLF/MAINT'.Access path maintenance (MAINT)
:P.When the access path is kept up to date&colon. as records change,
when the file is opened, or later.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *REBLD, *DLY.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGLF/RECOVER'.Access path recovery (RECOVER)
:P.When a damaged access path is rebuilt&colon. during the IPL, after
it, or when the file is next opened.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*IPL:EPK.
:PD.During the IPL.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *AFTIPL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGLF/FRCACCPTH'.Force keyed access path (FRCACCPTH)
:P.Whether access path changes are written to auxiliary storage with
each record change.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGLF/UNIT'.Preferred storage unit (UNIT)
:P.The preferred storage unit. The system places objects itself; the
value is kept.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGLF/FRCRATIO'.Records to force a write (FRCRATIO)
:P.How many records are written before they are forced to auxiliary
storage.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGLF/WAITFILE'.Maximum file wait time (WAITFILE)
:P.How many seconds the program waits for the file's resources to become
available when the file is opened. *IMMED does not wait; *CLS uses the
job's class.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.The program does not wait.
:PT.:PK.*CLS:EPK.
:PD.The default wait time of the job's class.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGLF/WAITRCD'.Maximum record wait time (WAITRCD)
:P.How many seconds the program waits for a record that another job has
locked.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGLF/SHARE'.Share open data path (SHARE)
:P.Whether the open data path of the file is shared with other programs
of the job that open it with SHARE(*YES)&colon. they then share the
file's position and buffers.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The program gets an open data path of its own.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The open data path is shared.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGLF/LVLCHK'.Record format level check (LVLCHK)
:P.Whether the record format level identifiers of the file are checked
against those the program was compiled with when the file is opened.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The level identifiers are checked.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.They are not checked.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGLF/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The text does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGPF.Change Physical File (CHGPF)
:P.Use the Change Physical File (CHGPF) command to change a physical
file's attributes, or its format from new DDS source.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/SRCFILE'.Source file (SRCFILE)
:P.The source physical file that holds the source member, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/SRCMBR'.Source member (SRCMBR)
:P.The member of the source file that holds the source. *PGM, *MODULE or
*CMD and the like mean the member with the same name as the object being
created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/OPTION'.Source listing options (OPTION)
:P.The source listing options for this command.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRC:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*SOURCE:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*NOSRC:EPK.
:PD.No source listing.
:PT.:PK.*NOSOURCE:EPK.
:PD.No source listing.
:PT.:PK.*LIST:EPK.
:PD.A list is shown.
:PT.:PK.*NOLIST:EPK.
:PD.No list.
:PT.:PK.*SECLVL:EPK.
:PD.With the second-level text of the messages.
:PT.:PK.*NOSECLVL:EPK.
:PD.Without the second-level text of the messages.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *EVENTF, *NOEVENTF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/GENLVL'.Generation severity level (GENLVL)
:P.The severity of the compile messages at or above which the object is
not created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 30.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 20 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/FLAG'.Flagging severity level (FLAG)
:P.The lowest severity of the messages the compiler lists.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 30.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/SYSTEM'.System (SYSTEM)
:P.The system for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LCL:EPK.
:PD.Local.
:PT.:PK.*RMT:EPK.
:PD.Remote.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FILETYPE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/EXPDATE'.Expiration date for member (EXPDATE)
:P.The date after which the object or file can be deleted or
overwritten. *PERM means it never expires.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.It never expires.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/MAXMBRS'.Maximum members (MAXMBRS)
:P.The largest number of members the file can hold.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/ACCPTHSIZ'.Access path size (ACCPTHSIZ)
:P.The largest size the file's access paths can reach.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MAX1TB, *MAX4GB.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/PAGESIZE'.Access path logical page size (PAGESIZE)
:P.The size of a page of the keyed access path, in kilobytes.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *KEYLEN.
:P.The value must be 8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256, 512.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/MAINT'.Access path maintenance (MAINT)
:P.When the access path is kept up to date&colon. as records change,
when the file is opened, or later.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *REBLD, *DLY.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/RECOVER'.Access path recovery (RECOVER)
:P.When a damaged access path is rebuilt&colon. during the IPL, after
it, or when the file is next opened.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*IPL:EPK.
:PD.During the IPL.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *AFTIPL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/FRCACCPTH'.Force keyed access path (FRCACCPTH)
:P.Whether access path changes are written to auxiliary storage with
each record change.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/SIZE'.Member size (SIZE)
:P.The member size for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Initial records
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 10 digits. The value must be from 1 to
2147483646.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Increment records
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 0 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Maximum increments
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 0 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/ALLOCATE'.Allocate storage (ALLOCATE)
:P.Whether the member's storage is allocated when the member is created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/UNIT'.Preferred storage unit (UNIT)
:P.The preferred storage unit. The system places objects itself; the
value is kept.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/FRCRATIO'.Records to force a write (FRCRATIO)
:P.How many records are written before they are forced to auxiliary
storage.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/WAITFILE'.Maximum file wait time (WAITFILE)
:P.How many seconds the program waits for the file's resources to become
available when the file is opened. *IMMED does not wait; *CLS uses the
job's class.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.The program does not wait.
:PT.:PK.*CLS:EPK.
:PD.The default wait time of the job's class.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/WAITRCD'.Maximum record wait time (WAITRCD)
:P.How many seconds the program waits for a record that another job has
locked.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/SHARE'.Share open data path (SHARE)
:P.Whether the open data path of the file is shared with other programs
of the job that open it with SHARE(*YES)&colon. they then share the
file's position and buffers.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The program gets an open data path of its own.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The open data path is shared.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/DLTPCT'.Max % deleted records allowed (DLTPCT)
:P.The highest percentage of deleted records the member may hold before
a message is sent.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 100.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/REUSEDLT'.Reuse deleted records (REUSEDLT)
:P.The reuse deleted records for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/SRTSEQ'.Sort sequence (SRTSEQ)
:P.The sort sequence table that orders and compares character
data&colon. the hexadecimal values, the job's, a language's (shared or
unique weights), or a table by name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SRC:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDSHR:EPK.
:PD.The shared-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. upper and
lower case compare equal.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDUNQ:EPK.
:PD.The unique-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. every
character has its own weight.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/LANGID'.Language identifier (LANGID)
:P.The language identifier&colon. three letters naming the language
whose sort sequence is used.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*JOBRUN:EPK.
:PD.The value used while the job runs.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/CCSID'.Coded character set ID (CCSID)
:P.The coded character set identifier&colon. the code page and character
set the data is in, or is to be converted to.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/ALWUPD'.Allow update operation (ALWUPD)
:P.Whether records can be updated through this file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/ALWDLT'.Allow delete operation (ALWDLT)
:P.The allow delete operation for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/LVLCHK'.Record format level check (LVLCHK)
:P.Whether the record format level identifiers of the file are checked
against those the program was compiled with when the file is opened.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The level identifiers are checked.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.They are not checked.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/NODGRP'.Node group (NODGRP)
:P.The node group for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/PTNKEY'.Partitioning key (PTNKEY)
:P.The partitioning key for this command.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPF/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The text does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGPFCST.Change Physical File Constraint (CHGPFCST)
:P.Use the Change Physical File Constraint (CHGPFCST) command to enable
or disable constraints of a physical file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPFCST/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPFCST/CST'.Constraint (CST)
:P.The constraint for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 258 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CHKPND.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPFCST/STATE'.Constraint state (STATE)
:P.The constraint state for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ENABLED, *DISABLED.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPFCST/CHECK'.Verify constraint (CHECK)
:P.The verify constraint for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGPFM.Change Physical File Member (CHGPFM)
:P.Use the Change Physical File Member (CHGPFM) command to change a
physical file member's attributes.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPFM/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPFM/MBR'.Member (MBR)
:P.The member for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPFM/SRCTYPE'.Source type (SRCTYPE)
:P.The type of the source member&colon. CLLE, RPGLE, PF, CMD and so on.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPFM/EXPDATE'.Expiration date for member (EXPDATE)
:P.The date after which the object or file can be deleted or
overwritten. *PERM means it never expires.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.It never expires.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPFM/SHARE'.Share open data path (SHARE)
:P.Whether the open data path of the file is shared with other programs
of the job that open it with SHARE(*YES)&colon. they then share the
file's position and buffers.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The program gets an open data path of its own.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The open data path is shared.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPFM/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The text does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGPFTRG.Change Physical File Trigger (CHGPFTRG)
:P.Use the Change Physical File Trigger (CHGPFTRG) command to enable or
disable triggers of a physical file. A disabled trigger is kept but its
program is not called.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPFTRG/FILE'.Physical file (FILE)
:P.The physical file whose triggers change, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPFTRG/TRG'.Trigger (TRG)
:P.The trigger changed, by name; *ALL for every trigger of the file.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 258 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPFTRG/TRGLIB'.Trigger library (TRGLIB)
:P.The library of the trigger's name. A trigger name needs its library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPFTRG/STATE'.Trigger state (STATE)
:P.Whether the triggers are enabled or disabled. *SAME leaves them as
they are.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ENABLED, *DISABLED.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGPRTF.Change Printer File (CHGPRTF)
:P.Use the Change Printer File (CHGPRTF) command to change a printer
file's attributes.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/DEVTYPE'.Printer device type (DEVTYPE)
:P.The device type.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SCS:EPK.
:PD.SCS, the SNA character string printer data.
:PT.:PK.*IPDS:EPK.
:PD.IPDS, the intelligent printer data stream.
:PT.:PK.*USERASCII:EPK.
:PD.ASCII data the user's application formatted.
:PT.:PK.*AFPDS:EPK.
:PD.AFP data.
:PT.:PK.*LINE:EPK.
:PD.Line data.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *AFPDSLINE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/PAGESIZE'.Page size (PAGESIZE)
:P.The size of a page of the keyed access path, in kilobytes.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Length
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 7 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 66 is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Width
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 7 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 1 to 378.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 132 is used.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Measurement method
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ROWCOL, *UOM.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/LPI'.Lines per inch (LPI)
:P.The lines per inch for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.The value must be 3, 4, 6, 7.5, 8, 9, 12.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/CPI'.Characters per inch (CPI)
:P.The characters per inch for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.The value must be 5, 10, 12, 13.3, 15, 16.7, 18, 20.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/FRONTMGN'.Front margin (FRONTMGN)
:P.The front margin for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Offset down
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 57.790.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Offset across
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 57.790.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/BACKMGN'.Back margin (BACKMGN)
:P.The back margin for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FRONTMGN.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Offset down
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 57.790.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Offset across
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 57.790.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/OVRFLW'.Overflow line number (OVRFLW)
:P.The overflow line number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/FOLD'.Fold records (FOLD)
:P.The fold records for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/RPLUNPRT'.Replace unprintable characters (RPLUNPRT)
:P.The replace unprintable characters for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Replace
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Replacement character
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 1 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, ' ' is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/ALIGN'.Align page (ALIGN)
:P.Whether the writer stops on the first page so the forms can be
aligned.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/CTLCHAR'.Control character (CTLCHAR)
:P.The control characters in the data&colon. none, or the first
character of each record as a FORTRAN control character.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*FCFC:EPK.
:PD.The first character of each record is a FORTRAN forms control
character.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MACHINE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/CHLVAL'.Channel values (CHLVAL)
:P.The lines of the page that channels 1 to 12 skip to.
:P.Up to 12 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NORMAL:EPK.
:PD.Normal.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Channel
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 2 digits. The value must be from 1 to 12.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Line number
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/FONT'.Font (FONT)
:P.The font the printer uses.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*CPI:EPK.
:PD.Characters per inch.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Identifier
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Point size
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 4 digits, 1 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0.1 to 999.9.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/FORMFEED'.Form feed (FORMFEED)
:P.How paper is fed to the printer&colon. continuous forms, cut sheets
fed by hand, or an automatic sheet feeder.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:PT.:PK.*CONT:EPK.
:PD.Continuous forms.
:PT.:PK.*CUT:EPK.
:PD.Single cut sheets fed by hand.
:PT.:PK.*AUTOCUT:EPK.
:PD.Single cut sheets from a sheet feeder.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CONT2.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/DRAWER'.Source drawer (DRAWER)
:P.The paper drawer the output is printed from.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *E1, *FORMDF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/OUTBIN'.Output bin (OUTBIN)
:P.The output bin the printed pages go to.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/PRTQLTY'.Print quality (PRTQLTY)
:P.The print quality&colon. draft, normal text or near-letter quality.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*STD:EPK.
:PD.Standard.
:PT.:PK.*DRAFT:EPK.
:PD.Draft quality.
:PT.:PK.*NLQ:EPK.
:PD.Near letter quality.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FASTDRAFT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/FORMTYPE'.Form type (FORMTYPE)
:P.The type of form the output is printed on. The writer stops for the
form to be loaded when it changes.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*STD:EPK.
:PD.Standard.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/COPIES'.Copies (COPIES)
:P.How many copies are printed.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/PAGRTT'.Degree of page rotation (PAGRTT)
:P.The degree of page rotation for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*AUTO:EPK.
:PD.Chosen automatically.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *COR.
:P.The value must be 0, 90, 180, 270.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/MULTIUP'.Pages per side (MULTIUP)
:P.The pages per side for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.The value must be 1, 2, 4.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/REDUCE'.Reduce output (REDUCE)
:P.The reduce output for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*TEXT:EPK.
:PD.Text.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/PRTTXT'.Print text (PRTTXT)
:P.Up to 30 characters printed at the bottom of every page of the job's
printed output.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 30 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/JUSTIFY'.Hardware justification (JUSTIFY)
:P.The hardware justification for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.The value must be 0, 50, 100.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/DUPLEX'.Print on both sides (DUPLEX)
:P.Whether the output prints on both sides of the paper.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *TUMBLE, *FORMDF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/UOM'.Unit of measure (UOM)
:P.The unit of measure for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *INCH, *CM.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/FRONTOVL'.Front side overlay (FRONTOVL)
:P.The front side overlay for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Overlay
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Offset down
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 57.790.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Offset across
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 57.790.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/BACKOVL'.Back side overlay (BACKOVL)
:P.The back side overlay for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FRONTOVL.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Overlay
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Offset down
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 57.790.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Offset across
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 57.790.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/SPOOL'.Spool the data (SPOOL)
:P.The spool the data for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/OUTQ'.Output queue (OUTQ)
:P.The output queue the spooled files go to.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*DEV:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/MAXRCDS'.Max spooled output records (MAXRCDS)
:P.The most records a spooled file may hold. *NOMAX sets no limit.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 6 digits. The value must be from 1 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/FILESEP'.File separators (FILESEP)
:P.How many separator pages print before each spooled file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 1 digits. The value must be from 0 to 9.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/SCHEDULE'.Spooled output schedule (SCHEDULE)
:P.When the spooled file can begin to print&colon. as soon as it is
created, when it is closed, or when the job ends.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*FILEEND:EPK.
:PD.When the file ends.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *JOBEND.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/HOLD'.Hold spooled file (HOLD)
:P.Whether the job or the spooled file is held until someone releases
it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.It is not held.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.It is held.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/SAVE'.Save spooled file (SAVE)
:P.The save spooled file for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/OUTPTY'.Output priority on OUTQ (OUTPTY)
:P.The priority of the job's spooled files on the output queue, from 1
(highest) to 9 (lowest).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 1 digits. The value must be from 1 to 9.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/USRDTA'.User data (USRDTA)
:P.User data, up to 10 characters, kept with the object.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SOURCE:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/SPLFOWN'.Spooled file owner (SPLFOWN)
:P.The spooled file owner for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CURUSRPRF, *CURGRPPRF, *JOBGRPPRF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/USRDFNOPT'.User defined option (USRDFNOPT)
:P.Options that a user-defined print program can use.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/USRDFNDTA'.User defined data (USRDFNDTA)
:P.Data that a user-defined print program can use.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/USRDFNOBJ'.User defined object (USRDFNOBJ)
:P.An object that a user-defined print program can use.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Object
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Object type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*DTAARA:EPK.
:PD.Data areas.
:PT.:PK.*DTAQ:EPK.
:PD.Data queues.
:PT.:PK.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.Files&colon. physical, logical, display, printer, save, tape and DDM
files.
:PT.:PK.*PSFCFG:EPK.
:PD.Print services configurations.
:PT.:PK.*USRIDX:EPK.
:PD.User indexes.
:PT.:PK.*USRQ:EPK.
:PD.User queues.
:PT.:PK.*USRSPC:EPK.
:PD.User spaces.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/SPLFNAME'.Spooled file name (SPLFNAME)
:P.The spooled file name for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/IGCDTA'.DBCS data (IGCDTA)
:P.Whether the file holds double-byte character set data.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/WAITFILE'.Maximum file wait time (WAITFILE)
:P.How many seconds the program waits for the file's resources to become
available when the file is opened. *IMMED does not wait; *CLS uses the
job's class.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.The program does not wait.
:PT.:PK.*CLS:EPK.
:PD.The default wait time of the job's class.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/SHARE'.Share open data path (SHARE)
:P.Whether the open data path of the file is shared with other programs
of the job that open it with SHARE(*YES)&colon. they then share the
file's position and buffers.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The program gets an open data path of its own.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The open data path is shared.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/LVLCHK'.Record format level check (LVLCHK)
:P.Whether the record format level identifiers of the file are checked
against those the program was compiled with when the file is opened.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The level identifiers are checked.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.They are not checked.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRTF/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The text does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGQRYA.Change Query Attributes (CHGQRYA)
:P.Use the Change Query Attributes (CHGQRYA) command to change a job's
query attributes.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGQRYA/JOB'.Job name (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.User&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Number&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters. The value must be from 000000 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGQRYA/QRYTIMLMT'.Query processing time limit (QRYTIMLMT)
:P.The query processing time limit for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 2147352578.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGQRYA/DEGREE'.Parallel processing degree (DEGREE)
:P.The parallel processing degree for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*OPTIMIZE:EPK.
:PD.The system chooses the best way.
:PT.:PK.*MAX:EPK.
:PD.The largest value.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *IO, *NBRTASKS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGQRYA/ASYNCJ'.Asynchronous job usage (ASYNCJ)
:P.The asynchronous job usage for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*LOCAL:EPK.
:PD.This system.
:PT.:PK.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DIST.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGQRYA/APYRMT'.Apply CHGQRYA to remote (APYRMT)
:P.The apply CHGQRYA to remote for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGQRYA/QRYOPTLIB'.Query options file library (QRYOPTLIB)
:P.The query options file library for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGQRYA/QRYSTGLMT'.Query storage limit (QRYSTGLMT)
:P.The query storage limit for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 2147352578.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGSRCPF.Change Source Physical File (CHGSRCPF)
:P.Use the Change Source Physical File (CHGSRCPF) command to change a
source physical file's attributes.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSRCPF/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSRCPF/SYSTEM'.System (SYSTEM)
:P.The system for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LCL:EPK.
:PD.Local.
:PT.:PK.*RMT:EPK.
:PD.Remote.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FILETYPE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSRCPF/EXPDATE'.Expiration date for member (EXPDATE)
:P.The date after which the object or file can be deleted or
overwritten. *PERM means it never expires.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.It never expires.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSRCPF/MAXMBRS'.Maximum members (MAXMBRS)
:P.The largest number of members the file can hold.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSRCPF/ACCPTHSIZ'.Access path size (ACCPTHSIZ)
:P.The largest size the file's access paths can reach.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MAX1TB, *MAX4GB.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSRCPF/SIZE'.Member size (SIZE)
:P.The member size for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Initial records
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 10 digits. The value must be from 1 to
2147483646.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Increment records
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 0 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Maximum increments
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 0 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSRCPF/ALLOCATE'.Allocate storage (ALLOCATE)
:P.Whether the member's storage is allocated when the member is created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSRCPF/UNIT'.Preferred storage unit (UNIT)
:P.The preferred storage unit. The system places objects itself; the
value is kept.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSRCPF/FRCRATIO'.Records to force a write (FRCRATIO)
:P.How many records are written before they are forced to auxiliary
storage.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSRCPF/WAITFILE'.Maximum file wait time (WAITFILE)
:P.How many seconds the program waits for the file's resources to become
available when the file is opened. *IMMED does not wait; *CLS uses the
job's class.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.The program does not wait.
:PT.:PK.*CLS:EPK.
:PD.The default wait time of the job's class.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSRCPF/WAITRCD'.Maximum record wait time (WAITRCD)
:P.How many seconds the program waits for a record that another job has
locked.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSRCPF/SHARE'.Share open data path (SHARE)
:P.Whether the open data path of the file is shared with other programs
of the job that open it with SHARE(*YES)&colon. they then share the
file's position and buffers.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The program gets an open data path of its own.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The open data path is shared.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSRCPF/DLTPCT'.Max % deleted records allowed (DLTPCT)
:P.The highest percentage of deleted records the member may hold before
a message is sent.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 100.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSRCPF/CCSID'.Coded character set ID (CCSID)
:P.The coded character set identifier&colon. the code page and character
set the data is in, or is to be converted to.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSRCPF/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The text does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CLOF.Close File (CLOF)
:P.Use the Close File (CLOF) command to close a file opened by OPNQRYF
or OPNDBF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CLOF/OPNID'.Open file identifier (OPNID)
:P.The open file identifier the file was opened with.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CLRPFM.Clear Physical File Member (CLRPFM)
:P.Use the Clear Physical File Member (CLRPFM) command to remove every
record from a physical file member.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CLRPFM/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CLRPFM/MBR'.Member (MBR)
:P.The member for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=COMMIT.Commit (COMMIT)
:P.Use the Commit (COMMIT) command to commit the current transaction.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='COMMIT/CMTID'.Commit identifier (CMTID)
:P.The commit identifier for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 4000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CPYF.Copy File (CPYF)
:P.Use the Copy File (CPYF) command to copy records between files, with
selection, mapping and printing.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYF/FROMFILE'.From file (FROMFILE)
:P.The file the data comes from.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYF/TOFILE'.To file (TOFILE)
:P.The file that receives the data.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed&colon. it goes to a spooled file of the job.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYF/FROMMBR'.From member (FROMMBR)
:P.The member the data comes from.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYF/TOMBR'.To member or label (TOMBR)
:P.The member of the to-file that receives the data.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FROMMBR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYF/MBROPT'.Replace or add records (MBROPT)
:P.What happens to an existing member that receives data&colon. its
records are replaced, or the new records are added after them.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The new entries are added to what is there.
:PT.:PK.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.What is there is replaced.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *UPDADD.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYF/CRTFILE'.Create file (CRTFILE)
:P.Whether to create file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYF/OUTFMT'.Print format (OUTFMT)
:P.The format of the output.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CHAR:EPK.
:PD.Character.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYF/PRINT'.Print records (PRINT)
:P.The print records for this command.
:P.Up to 3 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *EXCLD, *COPIED, *ERROR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYF/RCDFMT'.Record format of logical file (RCDFMT)
:P.The record format.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYF/FROMRCD'.From record number (FROMRCD)
:P.The from record number for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 10 digits. The value must be greater than 0.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *START.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYF/TORCD'.To record number (TORCD)
:P.The to record number for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*END:EPK.
:PD.The end.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 10 digits. The value must be greater than 0.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYF/FROMKEY'.From record key (FROMKEY)
:P.The from record key for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Number of key fields
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 120.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *BLDKEY.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Key value
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYF/TOKEY'.To record key (TOKEY)
:P.The to record key for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Number of key fields
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 120.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *BLDKEY.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Key value
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYF/NBRRCDS'.Number of records to copy (NBRRCDS)
:P.The number of records to copy for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*END:EPK.
:PD.The end.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 10 digits. The value must be greater than 0.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYF/INCCHAR'.Include by character test (INCCHAR)
:P.The include by character test for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 4 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Field or *RCD
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*RCD:EPK.
:PD.The record.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Starting position
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32766.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Relation
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*EQ:EPK.
:PD.Equal to.
:PT.:PK.*GT:EPK.
:PD.Greater than.
:PT.:PK.*LT:EPK.
:PD.Less than.
:PT.:PK.*NE:EPK.
:PD.Not equal to.
:PT.:PK.*GE:EPK.
:PD.Greater than or equal to.
:PT.:PK.*LE:EPK.
:PD.Less than or equal to.
:PT.:PK.*NG:EPK.
:PD.Not greater than.
:PT.:PK.*NL:EPK.
:PD.Not less than.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CT.
:H4.Part 4&colon. Value
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYF/INCREL'.Include by field test (INCREL)
:P.The include by field test for this command.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 4 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Logical operator
:P.Also accepted&colon. *IF, *AND, *OR.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Field
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Relation
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*EQ:EPK.
:PD.Equal to.
:PT.:PK.*GT:EPK.
:PD.Greater than.
:PT.:PK.*LT:EPK.
:PD.Less than.
:PT.:PK.*NE:EPK.
:PD.Not equal to.
:PT.:PK.*GE:EPK.
:PD.Greater than or equal to.
:PT.:PK.*LE:EPK.
:PD.Less than or equal to.
:PT.:PK.*NG:EPK.
:PD.Not greater than.
:PT.:PK.*NL:EPK.
:PD.Not less than.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CT.
:H4.Part 4&colon. Value
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYF/FMTOPT'.Record format field mapping (FMTOPT)
:P.The record format field mapping for this command.
:P.Up to 3 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*DROP:EPK.
:PD.Dropped.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NOCHK, *CVTSRC, *MAP, *CVTFLOAT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYF/SRCOPT'.Source update options (SRCOPT)
:P.The source update options for this command.
:P.Up to 2 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DATE:EPK.
:PD.The date.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SEQNBR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYF/SRCSEQ'.Source sequence numbering (SRCSEQ)
:P.The source sequence numbering for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Starting number
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 6 digits, 2 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0.01 to 9999.99.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1.00 is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Increment
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 6 digits, 2 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0.01 to 9999.99.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1.00 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYF/ERRLVL'.Errors allowed (ERRLVL)
:P.The errors allowed for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 10 digits. The value must be from 0 to
4294967288.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYF/COMPRESS'.Compress out deleted records (COMPRESS)
:P.Whether to compress out deleted records.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CPYFRMIMPF.Copy From Import File (CPYFRMIMPF)
:P.Use the Copy From Import File (CPYFRMIMPF) command to copy a
delimited or fixed-format import file or stream file into a database
member.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMIMPF/FROMFILE'.From file (FROMFILE)
:P.The file the data comes from.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMIMPF/FROMSTMF'.From stream file (FROMSTMF)
:P.The from stream file for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMIMPF/TOFILE'.To file (TOFILE)
:P.The file that receives the data.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMIMPF/MBROPT'.Replace or add records (MBROPT)
:P.What happens to an existing member that receives data&colon. its
records are replaced, or the new records are added after them.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The new entries are added to what is there.
:PT.:PK.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.What is there is replaced.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMIMPF/FROMCCSID'.From CCSID (FROMCCSID)
:P.The CCSID the data is in.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
