:HELP NAME=CPYSRCF.Copy Source File (CPYSRCF)
:P.Use the Copy Source File (CPYSRCF) command to copy source members
between source files.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYSRCF/FROMFILE'.From file (FROMFILE)
:P.The file the data comes from.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYSRCF/TOFILE'.To file (TOFILE)
:P.The file that receives the data.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYSRCF/FROMMBR'.From member (FROMMBR)
:P.The member the data comes from.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYSRCF/TOMBR'.To member (TOMBR)
:P.The member of the to-file that receives the data.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FROMMBR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYSRCF/MBROPT'.Replace or add records (MBROPT)
:P.What happens to an existing member that receives data&colon. its
records are replaced, or the new records are added after them.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.What is there is replaced.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The new entries are added to what is there.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYSRCF/SRCCHGDATE'.Source change date (SRCCHGDATE)
:P.The source change date for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NEW:EPK.
:PD.A new one.
:PT.:PK.*OLD:EPK.
:PD.The old one.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYSRCF/SRCOPT'.Source update options (SRCOPT)
:P.The source update options for this command.
:P.Up to 2 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DATE:EPK.
:PD.The date.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SEQNBR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYSRCF/SRCSEQ'.Source sequence numbering (SRCSEQ)
:P.The source sequence numbering for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Starting number
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 6 digits, 2 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0.01 to 9999.99.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1.00 is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Increment
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 6 digits, 2 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0.01 to 9999.99.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1.00 is used.
:EHELP.
