:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDSPF/SRCFILE'.Source file (SRCFILE)
:P.The source physical file that holds the source member, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDSPF/SRCMBR'.Source member (SRCMBR)
:P.The member of the source file that holds the source. *PGM, *MODULE or
*CMD and the like mean the member with the same name as the object being
created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDSPF/GENLVL'.Generation severity level (GENLVL)
:P.The severity of the compile messages at or above which the object is
not created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 30.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 20 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDSPF/FLAG'.Flagging severity level (FLAG)
:P.The lowest severity of the messages the compiler lists.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 30.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDSPF/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*REQUESTER:EPK.
:PD.The user or device of the job that runs the command.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDSPF/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDSPF/OPTION'.Source listing options (OPTION)
:P.The source listing options for this command.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRC:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*SOURCE:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*NOSRC:EPK.
:PD.No source listing.
:PT.:PK.*NOSOURCE:EPK.
:PD.No source listing.
:PT.:PK.*LIST:EPK.
:PD.A list is shown.
:PT.:PK.*NOLIST:EPK.
:PD.No list.
:PT.:PK.*SECLVL:EPK.
:PD.With the second-level text of the messages.
:PT.:PK.*NOSECLVL:EPK.
:PD.Without the second-level text of the messages.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *EVENTF, *NOEVENTF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDSPF/MAXDEV'.Maximum devices (MAXDEV)
:P.The maximum devices for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 256.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDSPF/ENHDSP'.Enhanced display (ENHDSP)
:P.Whether to enhanced display.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDSPF/RSTDSP'.Restore display (RSTDSP)
:P.Whether to restore display.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDSPF/DFRWRT'.Defer write (DFRWRT)
:P.Whether to defer write.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDSPF/CHRID'.Character identifier (CHRID)
:P.The graphic character set and code page of the data.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:PT.:PK.*JOBCCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the job.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CHRIDCTL.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Graphic character set
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Code page
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDSPF/DECFMT'.Decimal format (DECFMT)
:P.The decimal format&colon. the character used for the decimal point
and how zeros print before it.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDSPF/SFLENDTXT'.Subfile end text (SFLENDTXT)
:P.The subfile end text for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PK.*MSG:EPK.
:PD.A message is sent.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDSPF/WAITFILE'.Maximum file wait time (WAITFILE)
:P.How many seconds the program waits for the file's resources to become
available when the file is opened. *IMMED does not wait; *CLS uses the
job's class.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.The program does not wait.
:PT.:PK.*CLS:EPK.
:PD.The default wait time of the job's class.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDSPF/WAITRCD'.Maximum record wait time (WAITRCD)
:P.How many seconds the program waits for a record that another job has
locked.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDSPF/DTAQ'.Data queue (DTAQ)
:P.The data queue, by name and library.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDSPF/SHARE'.Share open data path (SHARE)
:P.Whether the open data path of the file is shared with other programs
of the job that open it with SHARE(*YES)&colon. they then share the
file's position and buffers.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The program gets an open data path of its own.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The open data path is shared.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDSPF/LVLCHK'.Record format level check (LVLCHK)
:P.Whether the record format level identifiers of the file are checked
against those the program was compiled with when the file is opened.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The level identifiers are checked.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.They are not checked.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDSPF/AUT'.Public authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDSPF/REPLACE'.Replace file (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTLF.Create Logical File (CRTLF)
:P.Use the Create Logical File (CRTLF) command to create a logical file
over physical files from DDS source.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLF/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLF/SRCFILE'.Source file (SRCFILE)
:P.The source physical file that holds the source member, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLF/SRCMBR'.Source member (SRCMBR)
:P.The member of the source file that holds the source. *PGM, *MODULE or
*CMD and the like mean the member with the same name as the object being
created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLF/GENLVL'.Generation severity level (GENLVL)
:P.The severity of the compile messages at or above which the object is
not created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 30.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 20 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLF/FLAG'.Flagging severity level (FLAG)
:P.The lowest severity of the messages the compiler lists.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 30.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLF/FILETYPE'.File type (FILETYPE)
:P.The file type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SRC:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DATA.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLF/OPTION'.Source listing options (OPTION)
:P.The source listing options for this command.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRC:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*SOURCE:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*NOSRC:EPK.
:PD.No source listing.
:PT.:PK.*NOSOURCE:EPK.
:PD.No source listing.
:PT.:PK.*LIST:EPK.
:PD.A list is shown.
:PT.:PK.*NOLIST:EPK.
:PD.No list.
:PT.:PK.*SECLVL:EPK.
:PD.With the second-level text of the messages.
:PT.:PK.*NOSECLVL:EPK.
:PD.Without the second-level text of the messages.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *EVENTF, *NOEVENTF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLF/SYSTEM'.System (SYSTEM)
:P.The system for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LCL:EPK.
:PD.Local.
:PT.:PK.*RMT:EPK.
:PD.Remote.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FILETYPE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLF/DTAMBRS'.Physical file data members (DTAMBRS)
:P.The physical file data members for this command.
:P.Up to 32 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Physical file
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Members
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLF/MBR'.Member (MBR)
:P.The member for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLF/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLF/MAXMBRS'.Maximum members (MAXMBRS)
:P.The largest number of members the file can hold.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLF/ACCPTHSIZ'.Access path size (ACCPTHSIZ)
:P.The largest size the file's access paths can reach.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MAX1TB, *MAX4GB.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLF/PAGESIZE'.Access path logical page size (PAGESIZE)
:P.The size of a page of the keyed access path, in kilobytes.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *KEYLEN.
:P.The value must be 8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256, 512.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLF/MAINT'.Access path maintenance (MAINT)
:P.When the access path is kept up to date&colon. as records change,
when the file is opened, or later.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *REBLD, *DLY.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLF/RECOVER'.Access path recovery (RECOVER)
:P.When a damaged access path is rebuilt&colon. during the IPL, after
it, or when the file is next opened.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*IPL:EPK.
:PD.During the IPL.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *AFTIPL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLF/FRCACCPTH'.Force keyed access path (FRCACCPTH)
:P.Whether access path changes are written to auxiliary storage with
each record change.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLF/UNIT'.Preferred storage unit (UNIT)
:P.The preferred storage unit. The system places objects itself; the
value is kept.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLF/FRCRATIO'.Records to force a write (FRCRATIO)
:P.How many records are written before they are forced to auxiliary
storage.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLF/WAITFILE'.Maximum file wait time (WAITFILE)
:P.How many seconds the program waits for the file's resources to become
available when the file is opened. *IMMED does not wait; *CLS uses the
job's class.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.The program does not wait.
:PT.:PK.*CLS:EPK.
:PD.The default wait time of the job's class.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLF/WAITRCD'.Maximum record wait time (WAITRCD)
:P.How many seconds the program waits for a record that another job has
locked.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 60 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLF/SHARE'.Share open data path (SHARE)
:P.Whether the open data path of the file is shared with other programs
of the job that open it with SHARE(*YES)&colon. they then share the
file's position and buffers.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The program gets an open data path of its own.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The open data path is shared.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLF/SRTSEQ'.Sort sequence (SRTSEQ)
:P.The sort sequence table that orders and compares character
data&colon. the hexadecimal values, the job's, a language's (shared or
unique weights), or a table by name.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRC:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDSHR:EPK.
:PD.The shared-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. upper and
lower case compare equal.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDUNQ:EPK.
:PD.The unique-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. every
character has its own weight.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLF/LANGID'.Language identifier (LANGID)
:P.The language identifier&colon. three letters naming the language
whose sort sequence is used.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*JOBRUN:EPK.
:PD.The value used while the job runs.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLF/LVLCHK'.Record format level check (LVLCHK)
:P.Whether the record format level identifiers of the file are checked
against those the program was compiled with when the file is opened.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The level identifiers are checked.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.They are not checked.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLF/AUT'.Public authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTPF.Create Physical File (CRTPF)
:P.Use the Create Physical File (CRTPF) command to create a physical
file from DDS source or a record length.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/RCDLEN'.Record length (RCDLEN)
:P.The length of the records, in bytes.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32766.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/SRCFILE'.Source file (SRCFILE)
:P.The source physical file that holds the source member, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/SRCMBR'.Source member (SRCMBR)
:P.The member of the source file that holds the source. *PGM, *MODULE or
*CMD and the like mean the member with the same name as the object being
created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/GENLVL'.Generation severity level (GENLVL)
:P.The severity of the compile messages at or above which the object is
not created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 30.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 20 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/FLAG'.Flagging severity level (FLAG)
:P.The lowest severity of the messages the compiler lists.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 30.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/FILETYPE'.File type (FILETYPE)
:P.The file type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SRC:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DATA.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/MBR'.Member (MBR)
:P.The member for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/OPTION'.Source listing options (OPTION)
:P.The source listing options for this command.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRC:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*SOURCE:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*NOSRC:EPK.
:PD.No source listing.
:PT.:PK.*NOSOURCE:EPK.
:PD.No source listing.
:PT.:PK.*LIST:EPK.
:PD.A list is shown.
:PT.:PK.*NOLIST:EPK.
:PD.No list.
:PT.:PK.*SECLVL:EPK.
:PD.With the second-level text of the messages.
:PT.:PK.*NOSECLVL:EPK.
:PD.Without the second-level text of the messages.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *EVENTF, *NOEVENTF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/SYSTEM'.System (SYSTEM)
:P.The system for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LCL:EPK.
:PD.Local.
:PT.:PK.*RMT:EPK.
:PD.Remote.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FILETYPE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/EXPDATE'.Expiration date for member (EXPDATE)
:P.The date after which the object or file can be deleted or
overwritten. *PERM means it never expires.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.It never expires.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/MAXMBRS'.Maximum members (MAXMBRS)
:P.The largest number of members the file can hold.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be at least 1.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/ACCPTHSIZ'.Access path size (ACCPTHSIZ)
:P.The largest size the file's access paths can reach.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MAX1TB, *MAX4GB.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/PAGESIZE'.Access path logical page size (PAGESIZE)
:P.The size of a page of the keyed access path, in kilobytes.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *KEYLEN.
:P.The value must be 8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256, 512.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/MAINT'.Access path maintenance (MAINT)
:P.When the access path is kept up to date&colon. as records change,
when the file is opened, or later.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *REBLD, *DLY.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/RECOVER'.Access path recovery (RECOVER)
:P.When a damaged access path is rebuilt&colon. during the IPL, after
it, or when the file is next opened.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*IPL:EPK.
:PD.During the IPL.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *AFTIPL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/FRCACCPTH'.Force keyed access path (FRCACCPTH)
:P.Whether access path changes are written to auxiliary storage with
each record change.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/SIZE'.Member size (SIZE)
:P.The member size for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Initial records
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 10 digits. The value must be from 1 to
2147483646.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 10000 is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Increment records
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 0 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1000 is used.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Maximum increments
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 0 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 3 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/ALLOCATE'.Allocate storage (ALLOCATE)
:P.Whether the member's storage is allocated when the member is created.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/CONTIG'.Contiguous storage (CONTIG)
:P.Whether to contiguous storage.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/UNIT'.Preferred storage unit (UNIT)
:P.The preferred storage unit. The system places objects itself; the
value is kept.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/FRCRATIO'.Records to force a write (FRCRATIO)
:P.How many records are written before they are forced to auxiliary
storage.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/WAITFILE'.Maximum file wait time (WAITFILE)
:P.How many seconds the program waits for the file's resources to become
available when the file is opened. *IMMED does not wait; *CLS uses the
job's class.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.The program does not wait.
:PT.:PK.*CLS:EPK.
:PD.The default wait time of the job's class.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/WAITRCD'.Maximum record wait time (WAITRCD)
:P.How many seconds the program waits for a record that another job has
locked.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 60 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/SHARE'.Share open data path (SHARE)
:P.Whether the open data path of the file is shared with other programs
of the job that open it with SHARE(*YES)&colon. they then share the
file's position and buffers.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The program gets an open data path of its own.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The open data path is shared.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/DLTPCT'.Max % deleted records allowed (DLTPCT)
:P.The highest percentage of deleted records the member may hold before
a message is sent.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 100.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/REUSEDLT'.Reuse deleted records (REUSEDLT)
:P.Whether to reuse deleted records.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/SRTSEQ'.Sort sequence (SRTSEQ)
:P.The sort sequence table that orders and compares character
data&colon. the hexadecimal values, the job's, a language's (shared or
unique weights), or a table by name.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRC:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDSHR:EPK.
:PD.The shared-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. upper and
lower case compare equal.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDUNQ:EPK.
:PD.The unique-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. every
character has its own weight.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/LANGID'.Language identifier (LANGID)
:P.The language identifier&colon. three letters naming the language
whose sort sequence is used.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*JOBRUN:EPK.
:PD.The value used while the job runs.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/CCSID'.Coded character set ID (CCSID)
:P.The coded character set identifier&colon. the code page and character
set the data is in, or is to be converted to.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/ALWUPD'.Allow update operation (ALWUPD)
:P.Whether records can be updated through this file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/ALWDLT'.Allow delete operation (ALWDLT)
:P.Whether to allow delete operation.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/LVLCHK'.Record format level check (LVLCHK)
:P.Whether the record format level identifiers of the file are checked
against those the program was compiled with when the file is opened.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The level identifiers are checked.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.They are not checked.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/NODGRP'.Node group (NODGRP)
:P.The node group for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/PTNKEY'.Partitioning key (PTNKEY)
:P.The partitioning key for this command.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPF/AUT'.Public authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTPRTF.Create Printer File (CRTPRTF)
:P.Use the Create Printer File (CRTPRTF) command to create a printer
file, from DDS source or as a plain one.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/SRCFILE'.Source file (SRCFILE)
:P.The source physical file that holds the source member, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/SRCMBR'.Source member (SRCMBR)
:P.The member of the source file that holds the source. *PGM, *MODULE or
*CMD and the like mean the member with the same name as the object being
created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/GENLVL'.Generation severity level (GENLVL)
:P.The severity of the compile messages at or above which the object is
not created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 30.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 20 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/FLAG'.Flagging severity level (FLAG)
:P.The lowest severity of the messages the compiler lists.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 30.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/DEVTYPE'.Printer device type (DEVTYPE)
:P.The device type.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SCS:EPK.
:PD.SCS, the SNA character string printer data.
:PT.:PK.*IPDS:EPK.
:PD.IPDS, the intelligent printer data stream.
:PT.:PK.*USERASCII:EPK.
:PD.ASCII data the user's application formatted.
:PT.:PK.*AFPDS:EPK.
:PD.AFP data.
:PT.:PK.*LINE:EPK.
:PD.Line data.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *AFPDSLINE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/OPTION'.Source listing options (OPTION)
:P.The source listing options for this command.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRC:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*SOURCE:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*NOSRC:EPK.
:PD.No source listing.
:PT.:PK.*NOSOURCE:EPK.
:PD.No source listing.
:PT.:PK.*LIST:EPK.
:PD.A list is shown.
:PT.:PK.*NOLIST:EPK.
:PD.No list.
:PT.:PK.*SECLVL:EPK.
:PD.With the second-level text of the messages.
:PT.:PK.*NOSECLVL:EPK.
:PD.Without the second-level text of the messages.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *EVENTF, *NOEVENTF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/PAGESIZE'.Page size (PAGESIZE)
:P.The size of a page of the keyed access path, in kilobytes.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Length
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 7 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 66 is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Width
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 7 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 1 to 378.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 132 is used.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Measurement method
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ROWCOL, *UOM.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/LPI'.Lines per inch (LPI)
:P.The lines per inch for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value must be 3, 4, 6, 7.5, 8, 9, 12.
:P.When no value is given, 6 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/CPI'.Characters per inch (CPI)
:P.The characters per inch for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value must be 5, 10, 12, 13.3, 15, 16.7, 18, 20.
:P.When no value is given, 10 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/FRONTMGN'.Front margin (FRONTMGN)
:P.The front margin for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Offset down
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 57.790.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Offset across
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 57.790.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/BACKMGN'.Back margin (BACKMGN)
:P.The back margin for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FRONTMGN.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Offset down
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 57.790.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Offset across
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 57.790.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/OVRFLW'.Overflow line number (OVRFLW)
:P.The overflow line number for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 60 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/FOLD'.Fold records (FOLD)
:P.Whether to fold records.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/RPLUNPRT'.Replace unprintable characters (RPLUNPRT)
:P.The replace unprintable characters for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Replace
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Replacement character
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 1 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, ' ' is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/ALIGN'.Align page (ALIGN)
:P.Whether the writer stops on the first page so the forms can be
aligned.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/CTLCHAR'.Control character (CTLCHAR)
:P.The control characters in the data&colon. none, or the first
character of each record as a FORTRAN control character.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*FCFC:EPK.
:PD.The first character of each record is a FORTRAN forms control
character.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MACHINE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/CHLVAL'.Channel values (CHLVAL)
:P.The lines of the page that channels 1 to 12 skip to.
:P.Up to 12 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NORMAL:EPK.
:PD.Normal.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Channel
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 2 digits. The value must be from 1 to 12.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Line number
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/FONT'.Font (FONT)
:P.The font the printer uses.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CPI:EPK.
:PD.Characters per inch.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Identifier
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Point size
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 4 digits, 1 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0.1 to 999.9.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/FORMFEED'.Form feed (FORMFEED)
:P.How paper is fed to the printer&colon. continuous forms, cut sheets
fed by hand, or an automatic sheet feeder.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:PT.:PK.*CONT:EPK.
:PD.Continuous forms.
:PT.:PK.*CUT:EPK.
:PD.Single cut sheets fed by hand.
:PT.:PK.*AUTOCUT:EPK.
:PD.Single cut sheets from a sheet feeder.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CONT2.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/DRAWER'.Source drawer (DRAWER)
:P.The paper drawer the output is printed from.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *E1, *FORMDF.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/OUTBIN'.Output bin (OUTBIN)
:P.The output bin the printed pages go to.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/PRTQLTY'.Print quality (PRTQLTY)
:P.The print quality&colon. draft, normal text or near-letter quality.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*STD:EPK.
:PD.Standard.
:PT.:PK.*DRAFT:EPK.
:PD.Draft quality.
:PT.:PK.*NLQ:EPK.
:PD.Near letter quality.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FASTDRAFT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/FORMTYPE'.Form type (FORMTYPE)
:P.The type of form the output is printed on. The writer stops for the
form to be loaded when it changes.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*STD:EPK.
:PD.Standard.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/COPIES'.Copies (COPIES)
:P.How many copies are printed.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/PAGRTT'.Degree of page rotation (PAGRTT)
:P.The degree of page rotation for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*AUTO:EPK.
:PD.Chosen automatically.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *COR.
:P.The value must be 0, 90, 180, 270.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/MULTIUP'.Pages per side (MULTIUP)
:P.The pages per side for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value must be 1, 2, 4.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/REDUCE'.Reduce output (REDUCE)
:P.The reduce output for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*TEXT:EPK.
:PD.Text.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/PRTTXT'.Print text (PRTTXT)
:P.Up to 30 characters printed at the bottom of every page of the job's
printed output.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 30 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/JUSTIFY'.Hardware justification (JUSTIFY)
:P.The hardware justification for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value must be 0, 50, 100.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/DUPLEX'.Print on both sides (DUPLEX)
:P.Whether the output prints on both sides of the paper.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *TUMBLE, *FORMDF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/UOM'.Unit of measure (UOM)
:P.The unit of measure for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *INCH, *CM.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/FRONTOVL'.Front side overlay (FRONTOVL)
:P.The front side overlay for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Overlay
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Offset down
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 57.790.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Offset across
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 57.790.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/BACKOVL'.Back side overlay (BACKOVL)
:P.The back side overlay for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FRONTOVL.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Overlay
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Offset down
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 57.790.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Offset across
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 57.790.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/SPOOL'.Spool the data (SPOOL)
:P.Whether to spool the data.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/OUTQ'.Output queue (OUTQ)
:P.The output queue the spooled files go to.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*DEV:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/MAXRCDS'.Max spooled output records (MAXRCDS)
:P.The most records a spooled file may hold. *NOMAX sets no limit.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 6 digits. The value must be from 1 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 100000 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/FILESEP'.File separators (FILESEP)
:P.How many separator pages print before each spooled file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 1 digits. The value must be from 0 to 9.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/SCHEDULE'.Spooled output schedule (SCHEDULE)
:P.When the spooled file can begin to print&colon. as soon as it is
created, when it is closed, or when the job ends.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILEEND:EPK.
:PD.When the file ends.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *JOBEND.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/HOLD'.Hold spooled file (HOLD)
:P.Whether the job or the spooled file is held until someone releases
it.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.It is not held.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.It is held.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/SAVE'.Save spooled file (SAVE)
:P.Whether to save spooled file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/OUTPTY'.Output priority on OUTQ (OUTPTY)
:P.The priority of the job's spooled files on the output queue, from 1
(highest) to 9 (lowest).
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 1 digits. The value must be from 1 to 9.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/USRDTA'.User data (USRDTA)
:P.User data, up to 10 characters, kept with the object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SOURCE:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/SPLFOWN'.Spooled file owner (SPLFOWN)
:P.The spooled file owner for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CURUSRPRF, *CURGRPPRF, *JOBGRPPRF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/USRDFNOPT'.User defined option (USRDFNOPT)
:P.Options that a user-defined print program can use.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/USRDFNDTA'.User defined data (USRDFNDTA)
:P.Data that a user-defined print program can use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/USRDFNOBJ'.User defined object (USRDFNOBJ)
:P.An object that a user-defined print program can use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Object
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Object type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*DTAARA:EPK.
:PD.Data areas.
:PT.:PK.*DTAQ:EPK.
:PD.Data queues.
:PT.:PK.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.Files&colon. physical, logical, display, printer, save, tape and DDM
files.
:PT.:PK.*PSFCFG:EPK.
:PD.Print services configurations.
:PT.:PK.*USRIDX:EPK.
:PD.User indexes.
:PT.:PK.*USRQ:EPK.
:PD.User queues.
:PT.:PK.*USRSPC:EPK.
:PD.User spaces.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/SPLFNAME'.Spooled file name (SPLFNAME)
:P.The spooled file name for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/IGCDTA'.DBCS data (IGCDTA)
:P.Whether the file holds double-byte character set data.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/WAITFILE'.Maximum file wait time (WAITFILE)
:P.How many seconds the program waits for the file's resources to become
available when the file is opened. *IMMED does not wait; *CLS uses the
job's class.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.The program does not wait.
:PT.:PK.*CLS:EPK.
:PD.The default wait time of the job's class.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/SHARE'.Share open data path (SHARE)
:P.Whether the open data path of the file is shared with other programs
of the job that open it with SHARE(*YES)&colon. they then share the
file's position and buffers.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The program gets an open data path of its own.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The open data path is shared.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/LVLCHK'.Record format level check (LVLCHK)
:P.Whether the record format level identifiers of the file are checked
against those the program was compiled with when the file is opened.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The level identifiers are checked.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.They are not checked.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/AUT'.Public authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRTF/REPLACE'.Replace file (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTSRCPF.Create Source Physical File (CRTSRCPF)
:P.Use the Create Source Physical File (CRTSRCPF) command to create a
source physical file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRCPF/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRCPF/RCDLEN'.Record length (RCDLEN)
:P.The length of the records, in bytes.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 13 to 32766.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 92 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRCPF/IGCDTA'.DBCS data (IGCDTA)
:P.Whether the file holds double-byte character set data.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRCPF/MBR'.Member (MBR)
:P.The member for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRCPF/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRCPF/SYSTEM'.System (SYSTEM)
:P.The system for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LCL:EPK.
:PD.Local.
:PT.:PK.*RMT:EPK.
:PD.Remote.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FILETYPE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRCPF/EXPDATE'.Expiration date for member (EXPDATE)
:P.The date after which the object or file can be deleted or
overwritten. *PERM means it never expires.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.It never expires.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRCPF/MAXMBRS'.Maximum members (MAXMBRS)
:P.The largest number of members the file can hold.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRCPF/ACCPTHSIZ'.Access path size (ACCPTHSIZ)
:P.The largest size the file's access paths can reach.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MAX1TB, *MAX4GB.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRCPF/SIZE'.Member size (SIZE)
:P.The member size for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Initial records
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 10 digits. The value must be from 1 to
2147483646.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 10000 is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Increment records
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 0 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1000 is used.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Maximum increments
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 0 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 499 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRCPF/ALLOCATE'.Allocate storage (ALLOCATE)
:P.Whether the member's storage is allocated when the member is created.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRCPF/CONTIG'.Contiguous storage (CONTIG)
:P.Whether to contiguous storage.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRCPF/UNIT'.Preferred storage unit (UNIT)
:P.The preferred storage unit. The system places objects itself; the
value is kept.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRCPF/FRCRATIO'.Records to force a write (FRCRATIO)
:P.How many records are written before they are forced to auxiliary
storage.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRCPF/WAITFILE'.Maximum file wait time (WAITFILE)
:P.How many seconds the program waits for the file's resources to become
available when the file is opened. *IMMED does not wait; *CLS uses the
job's class.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.The program does not wait.
:PT.:PK.*CLS:EPK.
:PD.The default wait time of the job's class.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRCPF/WAITRCD'.Maximum record wait time (WAITRCD)
:P.How many seconds the program waits for a record that another job has
locked.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 60 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRCPF/SHARE'.Share open data path (SHARE)
:P.Whether the open data path of the file is shared with other programs
of the job that open it with SHARE(*YES)&colon. they then share the
file's position and buffers.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The program gets an open data path of its own.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The open data path is shared.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRCPF/DLTPCT'.Max % deleted records allowed (DLTPCT)
:P.The highest percentage of deleted records the member may hold before
a message is sent.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 100.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRCPF/CCSID'.Coded character set ID (CCSID)
:P.The coded character set identifier&colon. the code page and character
set the data is in, or is to be converted to.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRCPF/AUT'.Public authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DLTF.Delete File (DLTF)
:P.Use the Delete File (DLTF) command to delete a file, or every file
matching a generic name.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTF/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTF/SYSTEM'.System (SYSTEM)
:P.The system for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LCL:EPK.
:PD.Local.
:PT.:PK.*RMT:EPK.
:PD.Remote.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FILETYPE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTF/RMVCST'.Remove constraint (RMVCST)
:P.The remove constraint for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*KEEP:EPK.
:PD.Kept.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RESTRICT, *REMOVE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DLTOVR.Delete Override (DLTOVR)
:P.Use the Delete Override (DLTOVR) command to delete file overrides at
a call level.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTOVR/FILE'.File being overridden (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTOVR/LVL'.Level (LVL)
:P.The level for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ACTGRPDFN:EPK.
:PD.As the activation group defines it.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPCPCST.Display Check Pending Constraint (DSPCPCST)
:P.Use the Display Check Pending Constraint (DSPCPCST) command to
display the records that keep a constraint in check pending.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPCPCST/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPCPCST/CST'.Constraint (CST)
:P.The constraint for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 258 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPCPCST/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPDBR.Display Database Relations (DSPDBR)
:P.Use the Display Database Relations (DSPDBR) command to display the
files and members that depend on a file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPDBR/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPDBR/MBR'.Member (MBR)
:P.The member for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPDBR/RCDFMT'.Record format (RCDFMT)
:P.The record format.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPDBR/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:PT.:PK.*OUTFILE:EPK.
:PD.The output goes to the database file named by OUTFILE.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPDBR/OUTFILE'.File to receive output (OUTFILE)
:P.The database file that receives the output when OUTPUT(*OUTFILE) is
given. The file is created with the system's model format when it does
not exist.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPDBR/OUTMBR'.Output member options (OUTMBR)
:P.The member of the output file that receives the records, and whether
they replace the member's records or are added after them.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Member to receive output
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first member of the file. A member with the file's name is added
when the file has none.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Replace or add records
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.The member's records are cleared first.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The records are added after the member's records.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPFD.Display File Description (DSPFD)
:P.Use the Display File Description (DSPFD) command to display a file's
description.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPFD/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPFD/TYPE'.Type of information (TYPE)
:P.The type of information for this command.
:P.Up to 13 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*MBR:EPK.
:PD.The member.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *BASATR, *ATR, *ACCPTH, *MBRLIST, *SELECT, *SEQ,
*RCDFMT, *SPOOL, *JOIN, *TRG, *CST, *NODGRP.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPFD/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:PT.:PK.*OUTFILE:EPK.
:PD.The output goes to the database file named by OUTFILE.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPFD/FILEATR'.File attributes (FILEATR)
:P.The file attributes for this command.
:P.Up to 12 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*LF:EPK.
:PD.Line feed.
:PT.:PK.*SAVF:EPK.
:PD.A save file.
:PT.:PK.*TAPF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the tape file.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *BSCF, *CMNF, *DDMF, *DKTF, *DSPF, *ICFF, *MXDF,
*PF, *PRTF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPFD/OUTFILE'.File to receive output (OUTFILE)
:P.The database file that receives the output when OUTPUT(*OUTFILE) is
given. The file is created with the system's model format when it does
not exist.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPFD/OUTMBR'.Output member options (OUTMBR)
:P.The member of the output file that receives the records, and whether
they replace the member's records or are added after them.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Member to receive output
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first member of the file. A member with the file's name is added
when the file has none.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Replace or add records
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.The member's records are cleared first.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The records are added after the member's records.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPFD/SYSTEM'.System (SYSTEM)
:P.The system for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LCL:EPK.
:PD.Local.
:PT.:PK.*RMT:EPK.
:PD.Remote.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPFD/ASPDEV'.ASP device (ASPDEV)
:P.The auxiliary storage pool device the command works in&colon. the
system ASP and basic user ASPs, or an independent ASP group.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALLAVL:EPK.
:PD.Every available ASP device.
:PT.:PK.*CURASPGRP:EPK.
:PD.The ASP group of the job's current thread.
:PT.:PK.*SYSBAS:EPK.
:PD.The system ASP and the basic user ASPs.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPFFD.Display File Field Description (DSPFFD)
:P.Use the Display File Field Description (DSPFFD) command to display
the fields of a file's record formats.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPFFD/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPFFD/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:PT.:PK.*OUTFILE:EPK.
:PD.The output goes to the database file named by OUTFILE.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPFFD/OUTFILE'.File to receive output (OUTFILE)
:P.The database file that receives the output when OUTPUT(*OUTFILE) is
given. The file is created with the system's model format when it does
not exist.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPFFD/OUTMBR'.Output member options (OUTMBR)
:P.The member of the output file that receives the records, and whether
they replace the member's records or are added after them.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Member to receive output
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first member of the file. A member with the file's name is added
when the file has none.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Replace or add records
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.The member's records are cleared first.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The records are added after the member's records.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPFFD/SYSTEM'.System (SYSTEM)
:P.The system for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LCL:EPK.
:PD.Local.
:PT.:PK.*RMT:EPK.
:PD.Remote.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPFFD/ASPDEV'.ASP device (ASPDEV)
:P.The auxiliary storage pool device the command works in&colon. the
system ASP and basic user ASPs, or an independent ASP group.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALLAVL:EPK.
:PD.Every available ASP device.
:PT.:PK.*CURASPGRP:EPK.
:PD.The ASP group of the job's current thread.
:PT.:PK.*SYSBAS:EPK.
:PD.The system ASP and the basic user ASPs.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPOVR.Display Override (DSPOVR)
:P.Use the Display Override (DSPOVR) command to display the file
overrides in effect.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPOVR/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPOVR/MRGOVR'.Merged overrides (MRGOVR)
:P.Whether to merged overrides.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPOVR/LVL'.Level (LVL)
:P.The level for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ACTGRPDFN:EPK.
:PD.As the activation group defines it.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPOVR/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPPFM.Display Physical File Member (DSPPFM)
:P.Use the Display Physical File Member (DSPPFM) command to display the
records of a physical file member.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPFM/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPFM/MBR'.Member (MBR)
:P.The member for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPFM/FROMRCD'.From record (FROMRCD)
:P.The from record for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*END:EPK.
:PD.The end.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 10 digits. The value must be greater than 0.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=EDTCPCST.Edit Check Pending Constraints (EDTCPCST)
:P.Use the Edit Check Pending Constraints (EDTCPCST) command to edit the
constraints in check pending and their verification.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ENDCMTCTL.End Commitment Control (ENDCMTCTL)
:P.Use the End Commitment Control (ENDCMTCTL) command to end commitment
control; takes no parameters.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ENDDBMON.End Database Monitor (ENDDBMON)
:P.Use the End Database Monitor (ENDDBMON) command to end a database
monitor, writing what it holds.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDDBMON/JOB'.Job name (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.User&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Number&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDDBMON/MONID'.Monitor ID (MONID)
:P.The monitor ID for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDDBMON/COMMENT'.Monitor comment (COMMENT)
:P.The monitor comment for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 100 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=INZPFM.Initialize Physical File Mbr (INZPFM)
:P.Use the Initialize Physical File Mbr (INZPFM) command to initialize a
physical file member with default or deleted records.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INZPFM/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INZPFM/MBR'.Member (MBR)
:P.The member for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INZPFM/RECORDS'.Records to add (RECORDS)
:P.The records to add for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PK.*DLT:EPK.
:PD.Delete authority.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INZPFM/TOTRCDS'.Total number of records (TOTRCDS)
:P.The total number of records for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 10 digits. The value must be from 1 to
2147483646.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NXTINCR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=OPNQRYF.Open Query File (OPNQRYF)
:P.Use the Open Query File (OPNQRYF) command to open a query over one or
more files with selection, ordering, joins, grouping and mapped fields.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPNQRYF/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 32 values can be given.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. File
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Member
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Record format
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPNQRYF/OPTION'.Open options (OPTION)
:P.The open options for this command.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*UPD:EPK.
:PD.Update authority.
:PT.:PK.*DLT:EPK.
:PD.Delete authority.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *INP, *OUT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPNQRYF/FORMAT'.Format of open records (FORMAT)
:P.The format of open records for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPNQRYF/QRYSLT'.Query selection (QRYSLT)
:P.The query selection for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 2000 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, *ALL is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPNQRYF/KEYFLD'.Key field (KEYFLD)
:P.The key field for this command.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Field
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 21 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Order
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ASCEND, *DESCEND.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Absolute value
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SIGNED, *ABSVAL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPNQRYF/UNIQUEKEY'.Unique key fields (UNIQUEKEY)
:P.The unique key fields for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 120.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPNQRYF/JFLD'.Join field (JFLD)
:P.The join field for this command.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. From field
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 21 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. To field
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 21 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Join operator
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*EQ:EPK.
:PD.Equal to.
:PT.:PK.*GT:EPK.
:PD.Greater than.
:PT.:PK.*LT:EPK.
:PD.Less than.
:PT.:PK.*NE:EPK.
:PD.Not equal to.
:PT.:PK.*GE:EPK.
:PD.Greater than or equal to.
:PT.:PK.*LE:EPK.
:PD.Less than or equal to.
:PT.:PK.*NG:EPK.
:PD.Not greater than.
:PT.:PK.*NL:EPK.
:PD.Not less than.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPNQRYF/JDFTVAL'.Join with default values (JDFTVAL)
:P.The join with default values for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ONLYDFT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPNQRYF/JORDER'.Join file order (JORDER)
:P.The join file order for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PK.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPNQRYF/GRPFLD'.Group field (GRPFLD)
:P.The group field for this command.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 21 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPNQRYF/GRPSLT'.Group selection (GRPSLT)
:P.The group selection for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 2000 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, *ALL is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPNQRYF/MAPFLD'.Mapped field (MAPFLD)
:P.The mapped field for this command.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 6 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Mapped field
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Expression
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PK.*CHAR:EPK.
:PD.Character.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PK.*DATE:EPK.
:PD.The date.
:PT.:PK.*TIME:EPK.
:PD.The time.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ZONED, *PACKED, *BIN, *FLT, *TIMESTP, *VCHAR,
*VHEX, *GRAPHIC, *VGRAPHIC.
:H4.Part 4&colon. Length
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32766.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 5&colon. Decimal positions
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 2 digits. The value must be from 0 to 63.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 6&colon. CCSID
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPNQRYF/IGNDECERR'.Ignore decimal data errors (IGNDECERR)
:P.Whether to ignore decimal data errors.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPNQRYF/OPNID'.Open file identifier (OPNID)
:P.The open file identifier the file was opened with.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPNQRYF/SEQONLY'.Limit to sequential only (SEQONLY)
:P.The limit to sequential only for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Sequential only
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Records per buffer
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPNQRYF/COMMIT'.Commitment control active (COMMIT)
:P.The commitment control level&colon. whether changes are made in units
the program commits or rolls back, and which records are locked.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPNQRYF/OPNSCOPE'.Open scope (OPNSCOPE)
:P.The scope of the open&colon. the activation group, the call level or
the job.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ACTGRPDFN:EPK.
:PD.As the activation group defines it.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPNQRYF/DUPKEYCHK'.Duplicate key check (DUPKEYCHK)
:P.Whether to duplicate key check.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPNQRYF/ALWCPYDTA'.Allow copy data (ALWCPYDTA)
:P.Whether a copy of the data may be used to answer a query.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*OPTIMIZE:EPK.
:PD.The system chooses the best way.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPNQRYF/OPTIMIZE'.Performance optimization (OPTIMIZE)
:P.The level of optimization the code generator applies. Higher levels
run faster but are harder to debug.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 10 digits. The value must be from 1 to
2147483647.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ALLIO, *FIRSTIO, *MINWAIT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPNQRYF/OPTALLAP'.Optimize all access paths (OPTALLAP)
:P.Whether to optimize all access paths.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPNQRYF/SRTSEQ'.Sort sequence (SRTSEQ)
:P.The sort sequence table that orders and compares character
data&colon. the hexadecimal values, the job's, a language's (shared or
unique weights), or a table by name.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDSHR:EPK.
:PD.The shared-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. upper and
lower case compare equal.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDUNQ:EPK.
:PD.The unique-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. every
character has its own weight.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPNQRYF/LANGID'.Language identifier (LANGID)
:P.The language identifier&colon. three letters naming the language
whose sort sequence is used.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*JOBRUN:EPK.
:PD.The value used while the job runs.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPNQRYF/TYPE'.Type of open (TYPE)
:P.The type of open for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NORMAL:EPK.
:PD.Normal.
:PT.:PK.*PERM:EPK.
:PD.Permanent&colon. it never expires.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=OVRDBF.Override With Database File (OVRDBF)
:P.Use the Override With Database File (OVRDBF) command to override a
database file's name and open attributes for the programs that run after
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDBF/FILE'.File being overridden (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDBF/TOFILE'.Overriding to database file (TOFILE)
:P.The file that receives the data.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDBF/MBR'.Member (MBR)
:P.The member for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDBF/POSITION'.Starting position in file (POSITION)
:P.The starting position in file for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*END:EPK.
:PD.The end.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *START.
:P.The value has 4 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Retrieve order
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RRN, *KEYB, *KEYBE, *KEY, *KEYAE, *KEYA.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Record number or key fields
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 10 digits. The value must be from 1 to
4294967288.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Record format
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 4&colon. Key value
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDBF/RCDFMTLCK'.Record format lock (RCDFMTLCK)
:P.The record format lock for this command.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Record format
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Lock state
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SHRRD, *SHRNUP, *SHRUPD, *EXCLRD, *EXCL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDBF/FRCRATIO'.Records to force a write (FRCRATIO)
:P.How many records are written before they are forced to auxiliary
storage.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDBF/FMTSLR'.Format selector program (FMTSLR)
:P.The format selector program for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDBF/WAITFILE'.Maximum file wait time (WAITFILE)
:P.How many seconds the program waits for the file's resources to become
available when the file is opened. *IMMED does not wait; *CLS uses the
job's class.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.The program does not wait.
:PT.:PK.*CLS:EPK.
:PD.The default wait time of the job's class.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDBF/WAITRCD'.Maximum record wait time (WAITRCD)
:P.How many seconds the program waits for a record that another job has
locked.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDBF/SEQONLY'.Limit to sequential only (SEQONLY)
:P.The limit to sequential only for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Sequential only
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Records per buffer
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDBF/NBRRCDS'.Records retrieved at once (NBRRCDS)
:P.The records retrieved at once for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDBF/EOFDLY'.End of file delay (EOFDLY)
:P.The end of file delay for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 99999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDBF/LVLCHK'.Record format level check (LVLCHK)
:P.Whether the record format level identifiers of the file are checked
against those the program was compiled with when the file is opened.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The level identifiers are checked.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.They are not checked.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDBF/EXPCHK'.Expiration date check (EXPCHK)
:P.Whether to expiration date check.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDBF/INHWRT'.Inhibit write (INHWRT)
:P.Whether to inhibit write.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDBF/SECURE'.Secure from other overrides (SECURE)
:P.Whether the file is protected from overrides at earlier call levels.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDBF/SHARE'.Share open data path (SHARE)
:P.Whether the open data path of the file is shared with other programs
of the job that open it with SHARE(*YES)&colon. they then share the
file's position and buffers.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The program gets an open data path of its own.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The open data path is shared.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDBF/OPNSCOPE'.Open scope (OPNSCOPE)
:P.The scope of the open&colon. the activation group, the call level or
the job.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ACTGRPDFN:EPK.
:PD.As the activation group defines it.
:PT.:PK.*CALLLVL:EPK.
:PD.The call level.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDBF/OVRSCOPE'.Override scope (OVRSCOPE)
:P.The scope of the override&colon. the call level, the activation group
or the job.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ACTGRPDFN:EPK.
:PD.As the activation group defines it.
:PT.:PK.*CALLLVL:EPK.
:PD.The call level.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDBF/DSTDTA'.Distributed data (DSTDTA)
:P.The distributed data for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DATA, *BUFFER.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=OVRDSPF.Override with Display File (OVRDSPF)
:P.Use the Override with Display File (OVRDSPF) command to override a
display file's name for the programs that run after it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDSPF/FILE'.File being overridden (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DSPF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDSPF/TOFILE'.Overriding to display file (TOFILE)
:P.The file that receives the data.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDSPF/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*REQUESTER:EPK.
:PD.The user or device of the job that runs the command.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDSPF/RSTDSP'.Restore display (RSTDSP)
:P.Whether to restore display.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDSPF/DFRWRT'.Defer write (DFRWRT)
:P.Whether to defer write.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDSPF/LVLCHK'.Record format level check (LVLCHK)
:P.Whether the record format level identifiers of the file are checked
against those the program was compiled with when the file is opened.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The level identifiers are checked.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.They are not checked.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDSPF/SECURE'.Secure from other overrides (SECURE)
:P.Whether the file is protected from overrides at earlier call levels.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDSPF/OVRSCOPE'.Override scope (OVRSCOPE)
:P.The scope of the override&colon. the call level, the activation group
or the job.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ACTGRPDFN:EPK.
:PD.As the activation group defines it.
:PT.:PK.*CALLLVL:EPK.
:PD.The call level.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDSPF/SHARE'.Share open data path (SHARE)
:P.Whether the open data path of the file is shared with other programs
of the job that open it with SHARE(*YES)&colon. they then share the
file's position and buffers.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The program gets an open data path of its own.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The open data path is shared.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDSPF/OPNSCOPE'.Open scope (OPNSCOPE)
:P.The scope of the open&colon. the activation group, the call level or
the job.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ACTGRPDFN:EPK.
:PD.As the activation group defines it.
:PT.:PK.*CALLLVL:EPK.
:PD.The call level.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDSPF/WAITFILE'.Maximum file wait time (WAITFILE)
:P.How many seconds the program waits for the file's resources to become
available when the file is opened. *IMMED does not wait; *CLS uses the
job's class.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.The program does not wait.
:PT.:PK.*CLS:EPK.
:PD.The default wait time of the job's class.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRDSPF/WAITRCD'.Maximum record wait time (WAITRCD)
:P.How many seconds the program waits for a record that another job has
locked.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=OVRPRTF.Override with Printer File (OVRPRTF)
:P.Use the Override with Printer File (OVRPRTF) command to override a
printer file's name and attributes for the programs that run after it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/FILE'.File being overridden (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PRTF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/TOFILE'.Overriding to printer file (TOFILE)
:P.The file that receives the data.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/DEVTYPE'.Printer device type (DEVTYPE)
:P.The device type.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SCS:EPK.
:PD.SCS, the SNA character string printer data.
:PT.:PK.*IPDS:EPK.
:PD.IPDS, the intelligent printer data stream.
:PT.:PK.*USERASCII:EPK.
:PD.ASCII data the user's application formatted.
:PT.:PK.*AFPDS:EPK.
:PD.AFP data.
:PT.:PK.*LINE:EPK.
:PD.Line data.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *AFPDSLINE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/PAGESIZE'.Page size (PAGESIZE)
:P.The size of a page of the keyed access path, in kilobytes.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Length
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 7 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Width
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 7 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 1 to 378.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Measurement method
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ROWCOL, *UOM.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/LPI'.Lines per inch (LPI)
:P.The lines per inch for this command.
:P.The value must be 3, 4, 6, 7.5, 8, 9, 12.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/CPI'.Characters per inch (CPI)
:P.The characters per inch for this command.
:P.The value must be 5, 10, 12, 13.3, 15, 16.7, 18, 20.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/FRONTMGN'.Front margin (FRONTMGN)
:P.The front margin for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Offset down
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 57.790.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Offset across
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 57.790.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/BACKMGN'.Back margin (BACKMGN)
:P.The back margin for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FRONTMGN.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Offset down
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 57.790.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Offset across
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 57.790.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/OVRFLW'.Overflow line number (OVRFLW)
:P.The overflow line number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/FOLD'.Fold records (FOLD)
:P.Whether to fold records.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/RPLUNPRT'.Replace unprintable characters (RPLUNPRT)
:P.The replace unprintable characters for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Replace
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Replacement character
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 1 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, ' ' is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/ALIGN'.Align page (ALIGN)
:P.Whether the writer stops on the first page so the forms can be
aligned.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/CTLCHAR'.Control character (CTLCHAR)
:P.The control characters in the data&colon. none, or the first
character of each record as a FORTRAN control character.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*FCFC:EPK.
:PD.The first character of each record is a FORTRAN forms control
character.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MACHINE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/CHLVAL'.Channel values (CHLVAL)
:P.The lines of the page that channels 1 to 12 skip to.
:P.Up to 12 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NORMAL:EPK.
:PD.Normal.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Channel
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 2 digits. The value must be from 1 to 12.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Line number
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/FONT'.Font (FONT)
:P.The font the printer uses.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*CPI:EPK.
:PD.Characters per inch.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Identifier
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Point size
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 4 digits, 1 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0.1 to 999.9.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/FORMFEED'.Form feed (FORMFEED)
:P.How paper is fed to the printer&colon. continuous forms, cut sheets
fed by hand, or an automatic sheet feeder.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:PT.:PK.*CONT:EPK.
:PD.Continuous forms.
:PT.:PK.*CUT:EPK.
:PD.Single cut sheets fed by hand.
:PT.:PK.*AUTOCUT:EPK.
:PD.Single cut sheets from a sheet feeder.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CONT2.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/DRAWER'.Source drawer (DRAWER)
:P.The paper drawer the output is printed from.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *E1, *FORMDF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/OUTBIN'.Output bin (OUTBIN)
:P.The output bin the printed pages go to.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/PRTQLTY'.Print quality (PRTQLTY)
:P.The print quality&colon. draft, normal text or near-letter quality.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*STD:EPK.
:PD.Standard.
:PT.:PK.*DRAFT:EPK.
:PD.Draft quality.
:PT.:PK.*NLQ:EPK.
:PD.Near letter quality.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FASTDRAFT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/FORMTYPE'.Form type (FORMTYPE)
:P.The type of form the output is printed on. The writer stops for the
form to be loaded when it changes.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*STD:EPK.
:PD.Standard.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/COPIES'.Copies (COPIES)
:P.How many copies are printed.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/PAGRTT'.Degree of page rotation (PAGRTT)
:P.The degree of page rotation for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*AUTO:EPK.
:PD.Chosen automatically.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *COR.
:P.The value must be 0, 90, 180, 270.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/MULTIUP'.Pages per side (MULTIUP)
:P.The pages per side for this command.
:P.The value must be 1, 2, 4.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/REDUCE'.Reduce output (REDUCE)
:P.The reduce output for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*TEXT:EPK.
:PD.Text.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/PRTTXT'.Print text (PRTTXT)
:P.Up to 30 characters printed at the bottom of every page of the job's
printed output.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 30 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/JUSTIFY'.Hardware justification (JUSTIFY)
:P.The hardware justification for this command.
:P.The value must be 0, 50, 100.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/DUPLEX'.Print on both sides (DUPLEX)
:P.Whether the output prints on both sides of the paper.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *TUMBLE, *FORMDF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/UOM'.Unit of measure (UOM)
:P.The unit of measure for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *INCH, *CM.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/FRONTOVL'.Front side overlay (FRONTOVL)
:P.The front side overlay for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Overlay
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Offset down
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 57.790.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Offset across
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 57.790.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/BACKOVL'.Back side overlay (BACKOVL)
:P.The back side overlay for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FRONTOVL.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Overlay
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Offset down
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 57.790.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Offset across
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits, 3 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 57.790.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/SPOOL'.Spool the data (SPOOL)
:P.Whether to spool the data.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/OUTQ'.Output queue (OUTQ)
:P.The output queue the spooled files go to.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*DEV:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/MAXRCDS'.Max spooled output records (MAXRCDS)
:P.The most records a spooled file may hold. *NOMAX sets no limit.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 6 digits. The value must be from 1 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/FILESEP'.File separators (FILESEP)
:P.How many separator pages print before each spooled file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 1 digits. The value must be from 0 to 9.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/SCHEDULE'.Spooled output schedule (SCHEDULE)
:P.When the spooled file can begin to print&colon. as soon as it is
created, when it is closed, or when the job ends.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*FILEEND:EPK.
:PD.When the file ends.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *JOBEND.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/HOLD'.Hold spooled file (HOLD)
:P.Whether the job or the spooled file is held until someone releases
it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.It is not held.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.It is held.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/SAVE'.Save spooled file (SAVE)
:P.Whether to save spooled file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/OUTPTY'.Output priority on OUTQ (OUTPTY)
:P.The priority of the job's spooled files on the output queue, from 1
(highest) to 9 (lowest).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 1 digits. The value must be from 1 to 9.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/USRDTA'.User data (USRDTA)
:P.User data, up to 10 characters, kept with the object.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SOURCE:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/SPLFOWN'.Spooled file owner (SPLFOWN)
:P.The spooled file owner for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CURUSRPRF, *CURGRPPRF, *JOBGRPPRF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/USRDFNOPT'.User defined option (USRDFNOPT)
:P.Options that a user-defined print program can use.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/USRDFNDTA'.User defined data (USRDFNDTA)
:P.Data that a user-defined print program can use.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/USRDFNOBJ'.User defined object (USRDFNOBJ)
:P.An object that a user-defined print program can use.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Object
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Object type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*DTAARA:EPK.
:PD.Data areas.
:PT.:PK.*DTAQ:EPK.
:PD.Data queues.
:PT.:PK.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.Files&colon. physical, logical, display, printer, save, tape and DDM
files.
:PT.:PK.*PSFCFG:EPK.
:PD.Print services configurations.
:PT.:PK.*USRIDX:EPK.
:PD.User indexes.
:PT.:PK.*USRQ:EPK.
:PD.User queues.
:PT.:PK.*USRSPC:EPK.
:PD.User spaces.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/SPLFNAME'.Spooled file name (SPLFNAME)
:P.The spooled file name for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/IGCDTA'.DBCS data (IGCDTA)
:P.Whether the file holds double-byte character set data.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/WAITFILE'.Maximum file wait time (WAITFILE)
:P.How many seconds the program waits for the file's resources to become
available when the file is opened. *IMMED does not wait; *CLS uses the
job's class.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.The program does not wait.
:PT.:PK.*CLS:EPK.
:PD.The default wait time of the job's class.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/SHARE'.Share open data path (SHARE)
:P.Whether the open data path of the file is shared with other programs
of the job that open it with SHARE(*YES)&colon. they then share the
file's position and buffers.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The program gets an open data path of its own.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The open data path is shared.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/LVLCHK'.Record format level check (LVLCHK)
:P.Whether the record format level identifiers of the file are checked
against those the program was compiled with when the file is opened.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The level identifiers are checked.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.They are not checked.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/SECURE'.Secure from other overrides (SECURE)
:P.Whether the file is protected from overrides at earlier call levels.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/OVRSCOPE'.Override scope (OVRSCOPE)
:P.The scope of the override&colon. the call level, the activation group
or the job.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ACTGRPDFN:EPK.
:PD.As the activation group defines it.
:PT.:PK.*CALLLVL:EPK.
:PD.The call level.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRPRTF/OPNSCOPE'.Open scope (OPNSCOPE)
:P.The scope of the open&colon. the activation group, the call level or
the job.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ACTGRPDFN:EPK.
:PD.As the activation group defines it.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=POSDBF.Position Database File (POSDBF)
:P.Use the Position Database File (POSDBF) command to position an open
database file at its start or end.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='POSDBF/OPNID'.Open file identifier (OPNID)
:P.The open file identifier the file was opened with.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='POSDBF/POSITION'.Position (POSITION)
:P.The position for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*END:EPK.
:PD.The end.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *START.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RGZPFM.Reorganize Physical File Mbr (RGZPFM)
:P.Use the Reorganize Physical File Mbr (RGZPFM) command to reorganize a
physical file member, dropping deleted records and optionally reordering
by a key.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RGZPFM/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RGZPFM/MBR'.Member (MBR)
:P.The member for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RGZPFM/KEYFILE'.Key file (KEYFILE)
:P.The key file for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RPLDLTRCD.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RGZPFM/SRCOPT'.Source update options (SRCOPT)
:P.The source update options for this command.
:P.Up to 2 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SEQNBR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RGZPFM/SRCSEQ'.Source sequence numbering (SRCSEQ)
:P.The source sequence numbering for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Starting number
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 6 digits, 2 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0.01 to 9999.99.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1.00 is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Increment
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 6 digits, 2 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0.01 to 9999.99.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1.00 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RGZPFM/ALWCANCEL'.Allow cancel (ALWCANCEL)
:P.Whether to allow cancel.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RGZPFM/LOCK'.Lock state (LOCK)
:P.The lock state for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *EXCL, *EXCLRD, *SHRUPD.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RGZPFM/RBDACCPTH'.Rebuild access paths (RBDACCPTH)
:P.The rebuild access paths for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*OPTIMIZE:EPK.
:PD.The system chooses the best way.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVM.Remove Member (RMVM)
:P.Use the Remove Member (RMVM) command to remove one member, a generic
set or every member of a file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVM/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVM/MBR'.Member (MBR)
:P.The member for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVM/RMVCST'.Remove constraint (RMVCST)
:P.The remove constraint for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*KEEP:EPK.
:PD.Kept.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RESTRICT, *REMOVE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVPFCST.Remove Physical File Constraint (RMVPFCST)
:P.Use the Remove Physical File Constraint (RMVPFCST) command to remove
constraints from a physical file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVPFCST/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVPFCST/CST'.Constraint (CST)
:P.The constraint for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 258 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CHKPND.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVPFCST/TYPE'.Constraint type (TYPE)
:P.The constraint type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *REFCST, *UNQCST, *PRIKEY, *CHKCST.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVPFCST/RMVCST'.Remove constraint (RMVCST)
:P.The remove constraint for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*KEEP:EPK.
:PD.Kept.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RESTRICT, *REMOVE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVPFTRG.Remove Physical File Trigger (RMVPFTRG)
:P.Use the Remove Physical File Trigger (RMVPFTRG) command to remove
triggers from a physical file&colon. one by name, or every trigger at a
time and for an event. The trigger programs are not deleted.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVPFTRG/FILE'.Physical file (FILE)
:P.The physical file the triggers are removed from, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVPFTRG/TRGTIME'.Trigger time (TRGTIME)
:P.The time of the triggers removed when no trigger name is given; *ALL
for both.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*BEFORE:EPK.
:PD.Before the reference entry.
:PT.:PK.*AFTER:EPK.
:PD.After the reference entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVPFTRG/TRGEVENT'.Trigger event (TRGEVENT)
:P.The event of the triggers removed when no trigger name is given; *ALL
for every event.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*DELETE:EPK.
:PD.Deleted.
:PT.:PK.*READ:EPK.
:PD.Read authority.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *INSERT, *UPDATE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVPFTRG/TRG'.Trigger (TRG)
:P.The trigger removed, by name; *ALL for the triggers TRGTIME and
TRGEVENT name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 258 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVPFTRG/TRGLIB'.Trigger library (TRGLIB)
:P.The library of the trigger's name; *ALL for any library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RNMM.Rename Member (RNMM)
:P.Use the Rename Member (RNMM) command to rename a member of a file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RNMM/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RNMM/MBR'.Member (MBR)
:P.The member for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RNMM/NEWMBR'.New member (NEWMBR)
:P.The new member for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ROLLBACK.Rollback (ROLLBACK)
:P.Use the Rollback (ROLLBACK) command to roll back the current
transaction; takes no parameters.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RUNSQL.Run SQL (RUNSQL)
:P.Use the Run SQL (RUNSQL) command to run one SQL statement given as a
string.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQL/SQL'.SQL statement (SQL)
:P.The SQL statement for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQL/COMMIT'.Commitment control (COMMIT)
:P.The commitment control level&colon. whether changes are made in units
the program commits or rolls back, and which records are locked.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*CHG:EPK.
:PD.Changed records are locked until committed.
:PT.:PK.*CS:EPK.
:PD.Cursor stability.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*RR:EPK.
:PD.Repeatable read.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NC, *UR, *RS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQL/NAMING'.Naming (NAMING)
:P.The naming for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYS:EPK.
:PD.The system's value.
:PT.:PK.*SQL:EPK.
:PD.SQL.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQL/DECMPT'.Decimal point (DECMPT)
:P.The decimal point for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*PERIOD:EPK.
:PD.A period.
:PT.:PK.*COMMA:EPK.
:PD.A comma.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQL/SRTSEQ'.Sort sequence (SRTSEQ)
:P.The sort sequence table that orders and compares character
data&colon. the hexadecimal values, the job's, a language's (shared or
unique weights), or a table by name.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDSHR:EPK.
:PD.The shared-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. upper and
lower case compare equal.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDUNQ:EPK.
:PD.The unique-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. every
character has its own weight.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQL/LANGID'.Language identifier (LANGID)
:P.The language identifier&colon. three letters naming the language
whose sort sequence is used.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*JOBRUN:EPK.
:PD.The value used while the job runs.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQL/DFTRDBCOL'.Default collection (DFTRDBCOL)
:P.The schema used for unqualified names in SQL statements with system
naming.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQL/DLYPRP'.Delay PREPARE (DLYPRP)
:P.Whether to delay PREPARE.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQL/ALWCPYDTA'.Allow copy of data (ALWCPYDTA)
:P.Whether a copy of the data may be used to answer a query.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*OPTIMIZE:EPK.
:PD.The system chooses the best way.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQL/ALWBLK'.Allow blocking (ALWBLK)
:P.The allow blocking for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*READ:EPK.
:PD.Read authority.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ALLREAD.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQL/SQLCURRULE'.SQL rules (SQLCURRULE)
:P.Whether DB2 or the standard SQL rules apply to the program's
statements.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*STD:EPK.
:PD.Standard.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DB2.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQL/DECRESULT'.Decimal result options (DECRESULT)
:P.The precision and scale of decimal results the program's SQL
statements compute.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Maximum precision
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 31 to 63.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 31 is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Maximum scale
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 63.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 31 is used.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Minimum divide scale
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 63.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQL/DECFLTRND'.DECFLOAT rounding mode (DECFLTRND)
:P.The DECFLOAT rounding mode for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *HALFEVEN, *UP, *DOWN, *CEILING, *FLOOR,
*HALFUP, *HALFDOWN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQL/CONACC'.Concurrent access (CONACC)
:P.The concurrent access for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CURCMT, *WAIT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQL/SYSTIME'.System time sensitive (SYSTIME)
:P.Whether to system time sensitive.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQL/OUTPUT'.Listing output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RUNSQLSTM.Run SQL Statements (RUNSQLSTM)
:P.Use the Run SQL Statements (RUNSQLSTM) command to run the SQL
statements of a source member or stream file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/SRCFILE'.Source file (SRCFILE)
:P.The source physical file that holds the source member, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/SRCMBR'.Source member (SRCMBR)
:P.The member of the source file that holds the source. *PGM, *MODULE or
*CMD and the like mean the member with the same name as the object being
created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/SRCSTMF'.Source stream file (SRCSTMF)
:P.The path of the stream file that holds the source. When it is given,
SRCFILE and SRCMBR are not used.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/COMMIT'.Commitment control (COMMIT)
:P.The commitment control level&colon. whether changes are made in units
the program commits or rolls back, and which records are locked.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CHG:EPK.
:PD.Changed records are locked until committed.
:PT.:PK.*CS:EPK.
:PD.Cursor stability.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*RR:EPK.
:PD.Repeatable read.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *UR, *RS, *NC.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/NAMING'.Naming (NAMING)
:P.The naming for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYS:EPK.
:PD.The system's value.
:PT.:PK.*SQL:EPK.
:PD.SQL.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/ERRLVL'.Severity level (ERRLVL)
:P.The severity level for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 40.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 10 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/DATFMT'.Date format (DATFMT)
:P.The format of dates&colon. the order of year, month and day.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*USA:EPK.
:PD.The USA format, mm/dd/yyyy or hh&colon.mm AM.
:PT.:PK.*ISO:EPK.
:PD.The ISO format, yyyy-mm-dd or hh.mm.ss.
:PT.:PK.*EUR:EPK.
:PD.The European format, dd.mm.yyyy or hh.mm.ss.
:PT.:PK.*JIS:EPK.
:PD.The Japanese industrial standard format, yyyy-mm-dd or
hh&colon.mm&colon.ss.
:PT.:PK.*MDY:EPK.
:PD.Month, day, year.
:PT.:PK.*DMY:EPK.
:PD.Day, month, year.
:PT.:PK.*YMD:EPK.
:PD.Year, month, day.
:PT.:PK.*JUL:EPK.
:PD.Julian&colon. year and day of the year.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/DATSEP'.Date separator (DATSEP)
:P.The character between the parts of a date.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 1 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/TIMFMT'.Time format (TIMFMT)
:P.The format of times.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*HMS:EPK.
:PD.Hours, minutes and seconds.
:PT.:PK.*USA:EPK.
:PD.The USA format, mm/dd/yyyy or hh&colon.mm AM.
:PT.:PK.*ISO:EPK.
:PD.The ISO format, yyyy-mm-dd or hh.mm.ss.
:PT.:PK.*EUR:EPK.
:PD.The European format, dd.mm.yyyy or hh.mm.ss.
:PT.:PK.*JIS:EPK.
:PD.The Japanese industrial standard format, yyyy-mm-dd or
hh&colon.mm&colon.ss.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/TIMSEP'.Time separator (TIMSEP)
:P.The character between the parts of a time.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 1 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/DFTRDBCOL'.Default collection (DFTRDBCOL)
:P.The schema used for unqualified names in SQL statements with system
naming.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/DECMPT'.Decimal point (DECMPT)
:P.The decimal point for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*PERIOD:EPK.
:PD.A period.
:PT.:PK.*COMMA:EPK.
:PD.A comma.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/SRTSEQ'.Sort sequence (SRTSEQ)
:P.The sort sequence table that orders and compares character
data&colon. the hexadecimal values, the job's, a language's (shared or
unique weights), or a table by name.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDSHR:EPK.
:PD.The shared-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. upper and
lower case compare equal.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDUNQ:EPK.
:PD.The unique-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. every
character has its own weight.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/LANGID'.Language identifier (LANGID)
:P.The language identifier&colon. three letters naming the language
whose sort sequence is used.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*JOBRUN:EPK.
:PD.The value used while the job runs.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/OUTPUT'.Listing output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/MARGINS'.Source margins (MARGINS)
:P.The source margins for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRCFILE:EPK.
:PD.The source file of the object.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 240.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/SECLVLTXT'.Second level text (SECLVLTXT)
:P.Whether to second level text.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/PROCESS'.Statement processing (PROCESS)
:P.The statement processing for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RUN, *SYN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/DLYPRP'.Delay PREPARE (DLYPRP)
:P.Whether to delay PREPARE.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/ALWCPYDTA'.Allow copy of data (ALWCPYDTA)
:P.Whether a copy of the data may be used to answer a query.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*OPTIMIZE:EPK.
:PD.The system chooses the best way.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/ALWBLK'.Allow blocking (ALWBLK)
:P.The allow blocking for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*READ:EPK.
:PD.Read authority.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ALLREAD.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/SQLCURRULE'.SQL rules (SQLCURRULE)
:P.Whether DB2 or the standard SQL rules apply to the program's
statements.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*STD:EPK.
:PD.Standard.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DB2.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/DECRESULT'.Decimal result options (DECRESULT)
:P.The precision and scale of decimal results the program's SQL
statements compute.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Maximum precision
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 31 to 63.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 31 is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Maximum scale
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 63.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 31 is used.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Minimum divide scale
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 63.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/DECFLTRND'.DECFLOAT rounding mode (DECFLTRND)
:P.The DECFLOAT rounding mode for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *HALFEVEN, *UP, *DOWN, *CEILING, *FLOOR,
*HALFUP, *HALFDOWN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/CONACC'.Concurrent access (CONACC)
:P.The concurrent access for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CURCMT, *WAIT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/SYSTIME'.System time sensitive (SYSTIME)
:P.Whether to system time sensitive.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/OPTION'.Listing option (OPTION)
:P.The listing option for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOLIST:EPK.
:PD.No list.
:PT.:PK.*LIST:EPK.
:PD.A list is shown.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNSQLSTM/TGTRLS'.Target release (TGTRLS)
:P.The release of the operating system the object is created for.
*CURRENT is this release; *PRV is the previous one.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.This release.
:PT.:PK.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=STRCMTCTL.Start Commitment Control (STRCMTCTL)
:P.Use the Start Commitment Control (STRCMTCTL) command to start
commitment control for the job or activation group.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRCMTCTL/LCKLVL'.Lock level (LCKLVL)
:P.The lock level for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*CHG:EPK.
:PD.Changed records are locked until committed.
:PT.:PK.*CS:EPK.
:PD.Cursor stability.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRCMTCTL/CMTSCOPE'.Commitment scope (CMTSCOPE)
:P.The commitment scope for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ACTGRP.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRCMTCTL/NFYOBJ'.Notify object (NFYOBJ)
:P.The notify object for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Object
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Object type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DTAARA, *MSGQ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRCMTCTL/DFTJRN'.Default journal (DFTJRN)
:P.The default journal for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRCMTCTL/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=STRDBMON.Start Database Monitor (STRDBMON)
:P.Use the Start Database Monitor (STRDBMON) command to start the
database monitor over a job or every job.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBMON/OUTFILE'.File to receive output (OUTFILE)
:P.The database file that receives the output when OUTPUT(*OUTFILE) is
given. The file is created with the system's model format when it does
not exist.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBMON/OUTMBR'.Output member options (OUTMBR)
:P.The member of the output file that receives the records, and whether
they replace the member's records or are added after them.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Member to receive output
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first member of the file. A member with the file's name is added
when the file has none.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Replace or add records
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.The member's records are cleared first.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The records are added after the member's records.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBMON/JOB'.Job name (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.User&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Number&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBMON/TYPE'.Type of records (TYPE)
:P.The type of records for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BASIC:EPK.
:PD.Basic.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DETAIL, *SUMMARY.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBMON/FRCRCD'.Force record write (FRCRCD)
:P.The force record write for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBMON/INLNBRRCD'.Initial number of records (INLNBRRCD)
:P.The initial number of records for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 2147483646.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBMON/RUNTHLD'.Run time threshold (RUNTHLD)
:P.The run time threshold for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 2147483647.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBMON/STGTHLD'.Storage threshold (STGTHLD)
:P.The storage threshold for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 2147483647.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBMON/INCSYSSQL'.Include system SQL (INCSYSSQL)
:P.The include system SQL for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *INI.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBMON/FTRFILE'.Filter by query file (FTRFILE)
:P.The filter by query file for this command.
:P.Up to 10 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBMON/FTRUSER'.Filter by user profile (FTRUSER)
:P.The filter by user profile for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBMON/FTRINTNETA'.Filter by internet address (FTRINTNETA)
:P.The filter by internet address for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*LOCAL:EPK.
:PD.This system.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 254 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBMON/FTRLCLPORT'.Filter by port number (FTRLCLPORT)
:P.The filter by port number for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBMON/FTRQRYGOVR'.Filter by query governor (FTRQRYGOVR)
:P.The filter by query governor for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *COND.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBMON/FTRCLTACG'.Filter by accounting string (FTRCLTACG)
:P.The filter by accounting string for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 128 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBMON/FTRCLTAPP'.Filter by application name (FTRCLTAPP)
:P.The filter by application name for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 128 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBMON/FTRCLTPGM'.Filter by program name (FTRCLTPGM)
:P.The filter by program name for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 128 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBMON/FTRCLTUSR'.Filter by client user ID (FTRCLTUSR)
:P.The filter by client user ID for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 128 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBMON/FTRCLTWS'.Filter by work station (FTRCLTWS)
:P.The filter by work station for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 128 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBMON/COMMENT'.Monitor comment (COMMENT)
:P.The monitor comment for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 100 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=STRSQL.Start SQL Interactive Session (STRSQL)
:P.Use the Start SQL Interactive Session (STRSQL) command to start the
interactive SQL session.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRSQL/COMMIT'.Commitment control (COMMIT)
:P.The commitment control level&colon. whether changes are made in units
the program commits or rolls back, and which records are locked.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CHG:EPK.
:PD.Changed records are locked until committed.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*CS:EPK.
:PD.Cursor stability.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*RR:EPK.
:PD.Repeatable read.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *UR, *NC, *RS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRSQL/NAMING'.Naming (NAMING)
:P.The naming for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYS:EPK.
:PD.The system's value.
:PT.:PK.*SQL:EPK.
:PD.SQL.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRSQL/PROCESS'.Statement processing (PROCESS)
:P.The statement processing for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RUN, *VLD, *SYN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRSQL/LIBOPT'.List libraries (LIBOPT)
:P.The list libraries for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LIB.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRSQL/DATFMT'.Date format (DATFMT)
:P.The format of dates&colon. the order of year, month and day.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*USA:EPK.
:PD.The USA format, mm/dd/yyyy or hh&colon.mm AM.
:PT.:PK.*ISO:EPK.
:PD.The ISO format, yyyy-mm-dd or hh.mm.ss.
:PT.:PK.*EUR:EPK.
:PD.The European format, dd.mm.yyyy or hh.mm.ss.
:PT.:PK.*JIS:EPK.
:PD.The Japanese industrial standard format, yyyy-mm-dd or
hh&colon.mm&colon.ss.
:PT.:PK.*MDY:EPK.
:PD.Month, day, year.
:PT.:PK.*DMY:EPK.
:PD.Day, month, year.
:PT.:PK.*YMD:EPK.
:PD.Year, month, day.
:PT.:PK.*JUL:EPK.
:PD.Julian&colon. year and day of the year.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRSQL/DATSEP'.Date separator (DATSEP)
:P.The character between the parts of a date.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 1 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRSQL/TIMFMT'.Time format (TIMFMT)
:P.The format of times.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*HMS:EPK.
:PD.Hours, minutes and seconds.
:PT.:PK.*USA:EPK.
:PD.The USA format, mm/dd/yyyy or hh&colon.mm AM.
:PT.:PK.*ISO:EPK.
:PD.The ISO format, yyyy-mm-dd or hh.mm.ss.
:PT.:PK.*EUR:EPK.
:PD.The European format, dd.mm.yyyy or hh.mm.ss.
:PT.:PK.*JIS:EPK.
:PD.The Japanese industrial standard format, yyyy-mm-dd or
hh&colon.mm&colon.ss.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRSQL/TIMSEP'.Time separator (TIMSEP)
:P.The character between the parts of a time.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 1 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRSQL/DECPNT'.Decimal point (DECPNT)
:P.The decimal point for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*PERIOD:EPK.
:PD.A period.
:PT.:PK.*COMMA:EPK.
:PD.A comma.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRSQL/PGMLNG'.Program language (PGMLNG)
:P.The program language for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *C, *CBL, *PLI, *RPG, *FTN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRSQL/SRTSEQ'.Sort sequence (SRTSEQ)
:P.The sort sequence table that orders and compares character
data&colon. the hexadecimal values, the job's, a language's (shared or
unique weights), or a table by name.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDSHR:EPK.
:PD.The shared-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. upper and
lower case compare equal.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDUNQ:EPK.
:PD.The unique-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. every
character has its own weight.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRSQL/LANGID'.Language identifier (LANGID)
:P.The language identifier&colon. three letters naming the language
whose sort sequence is used.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*JOBRUN:EPK.
:PD.The value used while the job runs.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRSQL/SQLSTRDLM'.SQL string delimiter (SQLSTRDLM)
:P.The SQL string delimiter for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *APOSTSQL, *QUOTESQL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRSQL/ALWCPYDTA'.Allow copy of data (ALWCPYDTA)
:P.Whether a copy of the data may be used to answer a query.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*OPTIMIZE:EPK.
:PD.The system chooses the best way.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRSQL/DFTRDBCOL'.Default collection (DFTRDBCOL)
:P.The schema used for unqualified names in SQL statements with system
naming.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRSQL/SQLCURRULE'.SQL rules (SQLCURRULE)
:P.Whether DB2 or the standard SQL rules apply to the program's
statements.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*STD:EPK.
:PD.Standard.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DB2.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRSQL/DECRESULT'.Decimal result options (DECRESULT)
:P.The precision and scale of decimal results the program's SQL
statements compute.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Maximum precision
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 31 to 63.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 31 is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Maximum scale
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 63.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 31 is used.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Minimum divide scale
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 63.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRSQL/DECFLTRND'.DECFLOAT rounding mode (DECFLTRND)
:P.The DECFLOAT rounding mode for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *HALFEVEN, *UP, *DOWN, *CEILING, *FLOOR,
*HALFUP, *HALFDOWN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRSQL/CONACC'.Concurrent access (CONACC)
:P.The concurrent access for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CURCMT, *WAIT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRSQL/SYSTIME'.System time sensitive (SYSTIME)
:P.Whether to system time sensitive.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKPFCST.Work with Physical File Constraints (WRKPFCST)
:P.Use the Work with Physical File Constraints (WRKPFCST) command to
work with the constraints of physical files.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKPFCST/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKPFCST/CST'.Constraint (CST)
:P.The constraint for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 258 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CHKPND.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKPFCST/TYPE'.Constraint type (TYPE)
:P.The constraint type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *REFCST, *UNQCST, *PRIKEY, *CHKCST.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
